{"parentUuid":"5fe5ddf9-aa81-40b7-a8a8-53dc9a98ab7b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMQa7smbG8ruUh6aUyof","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VJRzFR7FVb6vZ5xsf4w1mj","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Adversarial: release security","subagent_type":"bug-hunter","prompt":"You are a principal engineer doing an ADVERSARIAL review of \"Callisto\", a Rust CLI + GitHub Action that versions and releases polyglot workspaces (Cargo/npm/PyPI) from changesets. Repo: /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main (main, v0.14.2). Read ARCHITECTURE.md, AGENTS.md, docs/adr/ (esp. 2, 3, 4, 8), docs/architecture/release.md first. Product goal: a release tool teams can trust to publish to public registries from CI without leaking secrets, publishing the wrong thing, or being tricked by untrusted input.\n\nRULES: read-only. Do NOT edit/commit/push, do NOT run cargo build/test/publish/clippy, no network publishes. You may read, grep, and run the prebuilt binary /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/15c732d1/tmp/profile-target/release/callisto on scratch repos under a UNIQUE directory `$TMPDIR/adv-security-$$` (other agents run in parallel; never use a shared path, never rm outside your own dir). Never run git commands in the real repo except read-only `git log/show`.\n\nYOUR LENS: security and trust boundaries. Attack it: (1) the GitHub workflow/action design (.github/workflows/callisto-release.yml, .github/actions/*, scripts under .github/): untrusted PR content reaching a privileged job, expression/shell injection through branch names/PR titles/changeset text/package names/versions, artifact download trust between jobs, what `execute` trusts, token scopes, pull_request_target-style hazards, actions pinning; (2) the release intent/decision/receipt digest chain: what is bound and what is NOT (e.g. things outside the digest that influence effects: registry endpoints, publish args, notes, tag annotation), TOCTOU between plan and execute, replay of an old intent, a malicious committed decision file; (3) path containment and symlink handling in manifest/changelog/artifact paths, archive extraction, `..` in config paths (changelog, package dirs, artifact dirs); (4) command construction for cargo/npm/pnpm/twine/gh/git: argument injection from package names, versions, tags, registry URLs, dist-tags; env var leakage into child processes; credential redaction gaps (output, errors, JSON, receipts, logs); (5) supply chain of Callisto itself: the installer (.github/actions/setup-callisto, scripts), checksum/attestation verification, floating tags.\nFor each finding give: severity (critical/high/medium/low), exact file:line, a concrete attack or failure scenario, whether you REPRODUCED it (command + output) or only READ it, and a one-line fix direction. Rank by severity. Report at most the 12 most important findings; drop anything speculative that you cannot tie to code. Also list 3-5 things that are done WELL (so the owner knows what not to touch). Be concise and precise."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":532143,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":6842,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":784},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":532143,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6842,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":532143,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":532143},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":{"cache_miss_reason":{"type":"previous_message_not_found"}},"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01VJRzFR7FVb6vZ5xsf4w1m