and construction for cargo/npm/pnpm/twine/gh/git: argument injection from package names, versions, tags, registry URLs, dist-tags; env var leakage into child processes; credential redaction gaps (output, errors, JSON, receipts, logs); (5) supply chain of Callisto itself: the installer (.github/actions/setup-callisto, scripts), checksum/attestation verification, floating tags.\nFor each finding give: severity (critical/high/medium/low), exact file:line, a concrete attack or failure scenario, whether you REPRODUCED it (command + output) or only READ it, and a one-line fix direction. Rank by severity. Report at most the 12 most important findings; drop anything speculative that you cannot tie to code. Also list 3-5 things that are done WELL (so the owner knows what not to touch). Be concise and precise."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"10d5f8d8-491b-4598-ad2c-cfbc872079f4","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgMQa7Lm22WxaxCCcJtMp","requestRef":"101d988e-7ad2-4706-8aa6-f8712495b10b","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"1d634190-3821-4450-91f5-6fdf340df748","timestamp":"2026-10-24T16:51:23.487Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"chore/release-target-facts","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
{"parentUuid":"1d634190-3821-4450-91f5-6fdf340df748","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMQa7smbG8ruUh6aUyof","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018MkwufE7FStriGRXTAP3SY","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Adversarial: failure and recovery","subagent_type":"bug-hunter","prompt":"You are a principal engineer doing an ADVERSARIAL review of \"Callisto\", a Rust CLI + GitHub Action that versions and releases polyglot workspaces (Cargo/npm/PyPI) from changesets. Repo: /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main (main, v0.14.2). Read ARCHITECTURE.md, AGENTS.md, docs/adr/ (esp. 2, 3, 9, 12), docs/architecture/release.md and docs/specs/release.json first. Product goal: releases are irreversible effects on public registries; the tool must be safe to crash, rerun, run concurrently, and run on a flaky network, without publishing wrong code, tagging the wrong commit, or wedging a release.\n\nRULES: read-only. Do NOT edit/commit/push, do NOT run cargo build/test/publish/clippy, no network publishes. You may read, grep, and run the prebuilt binary /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/15c732d1/tmp/profile-target/release/callisto on scratch repos under a UNIQUE directory `$TMPDIR/adv-recovery-$$` (other agents run in parallel; never use a shared path, never rm outside your own dir). A fake `cargo`/`npm` on PATH inside your scratch dir is fine for exercising release flows locally (see crates/callisto-cli/tests/common/release_harness.rs for how tests do it). Never run git commands in the real repo except read-only `git log/show`.\n\nYOUR LENS: failure, recovery and concurrency semantics. Walk every effect (registry publish, tag create+push, GitHub release draft/upload/publish, release-PR commit) and ask: what if the process dies right before / right after / during it; what if the registry shows the version late, shows a DIFFERENT artifact, rate-limits, or returns 5xx; what if two runs overlap (CI re-run, two merges, local + CI); what if HEAD moves between plan and execute; what if a tag exists remotely but not locally or points elsewhere; what if the registry accepts the publish but the response is lost (non-idempotent effect with unknown outcome); partial multi-package/multi-registry releases and how a rerun adopts them (ADR 3); the E320 version-commit logic (crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/release/version_commit.rs) and the confirmation window / ConfirmationWave (release_execution.rs); fixed-group and dual-ecosystem packages; Python multi-file uploads; npm dist-tag outcomes; wall-clock and timeout handling; receipts. Find states that are unrecoverable, silently wrong, or that wedge a rerun with a misleading error.\nFor each finding give: severity, exact file:line, the concrete interleaving/scenario, whether you REPRODUCED it (command + output) or only READ it, and a one-line fix direction. Rank by severity. Report at most the 12 most important findings; drop speculation that you cannot tie to code. Also list 3-5 things done WELL. Be concise and precise."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":532143,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":6842,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":784},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":532143,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6842,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":532143,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":532143},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":{"cache_miss_reason":{"type":"previous_message_not_found"}},"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_018MkwufE7FStriGRXTAP3SY