ckage/multi-registry releases and how a rerun adopts them (ADR 3); the E320 version-commit logic (crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/release/version_commit.rs) and the confirmation window / ConfirmationWave (release_execution.rs); fixed-group and dual-ecosystem packages; Python multi-file uploads; npm dist-tag outcomes; wall-clock and timeout handling; receipts. Find states that are unrecoverable, silently wrong, or that wedge a rerun with a misleading error.\nFor each finding give: severity, exact file:line, the concrete interleaving/scenario, whether you REPRODUCED it (command + output) or only READ it, and a one-line fix direction. Rank by severity. Report at most the 12 most important findings; drop speculation that you cannot tie to code. Also list 3-5 things done WELL. Be concise and precise."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"10d5f8d8-491b-4598-ad2c-cfbc872079f4","apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011CgMQa7Lm22WxaxCCcJtMp","requestRef":"101d988e-7ad2-4706-8aa6-f8712495b10b","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"fc2b9e6a-d0de-450a-ab62-75523560c3be","timestamp":"2026-10-24T16:51:31.057Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"chore/release-target-facts","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
{"parentUuid":"fc2b9e6a-d0de-450a-ab62-75523560c3be","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMQa7smbG8ruUh6aUyof","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UNZMP58ThK9FgC1R376rUF","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Adversarial: versioning correctness","subagent_type":"bug-hunter","prompt":"You are a principal engineer doing an ADVERSARIAL review of \"Callisto\", a Rust CLI + GitHub Action that versions and releases polyglot workspaces (Cargo/npm/PyPI) from changesets. Repo: /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main (main, v0.14.2). Read ARCHITECTURE.md, AGENTS.md, docs/architecture/versioning.md, identity.md and docs/specs/versioning.json first. Product goal: `callisto version` rewrites manifests, lockfiles, changelogs and dependency ranges across ecosystems; a wrong rewrite means a broken or wrongly-versioned public package. It must preserve formatting and never corrupt a manifest.\n\nRULES: read-only on the repo. Do NOT edit/commit/push, do NOT run cargo build/test/publish/clippy, no network. You may read, grep, and run the prebuilt binary /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/15c732d1/tmp/profile-target/release/callisto on scratch repos under a UNIQUE directory `$TMPDIR/adv-version-$$` (other agents run in parallel; never use a shared path, never rm outside your own dir). Use `--no-refresh-lockfiles` where a lockfile refresh would need network. Never run git commands in the real repo except read-only `git log/show`.\n\nYOUR LENS: versioning and manifest-editing correctness. Attack: (1) format-preserving edits in crates/callisto-manifests and crates/callisto-graph/src/apply* (toml_edit, JSON key order/indentation, pyproject, setup.cfg, Cargo.lock/package-lock/pnpm-lock interactions): unusual manifests (comments, inline tables, dotted keys, CRLF, BOM, duplicate keys, workspace inheritance `version.workspace = true`, `[workspace.dependencies]`, `[patch]`, target-specific deps, renamed deps `package = \"x\"`, git/path deps, `publish = false`, npm `workspace:*`/`catalog:`/aliases `npm:`/overrides/peer/optional, PEP 440 specifiers with extras/markers, Poetry vs PEP 621 vs setuptools dynamic versions); (2) semver and PEP 440 handling: prerelease ordering, build metadata, 0.x rules, `none`/`patch` severities, pre mode enter/exit with dependents, snapshot versions; (3) cascade logic (crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade*): cycles, dev-dependency cycles, peer escalation, fixed/linked groups, a dependency range rewritten to one that excludes the new version, the 4n+1 bound; (4) changeset parsing (crates/callisto-model/src/format/changeset): frontmatter edge cases, unicode, huge files, duplicate entries, an entry naming the same package twice, summaries that could inject into generated markdown/PR bodies/workflow outputs; (5) changelog generation and idempotence (running `version` twice, partial failure leaving a half-written tree: is it atomic? see AGENTS.md invariants and callisto_model::atomic).\nFor each finding give: severity, exact file:line, a minimal input that triggers it, whether you REPRODUCED it (command + output) or only READ it, and a one-line fix direction. Rank by severity. Report at most the 12 most important findings; drop speculation you cannot tie to code. Also list 3-5 things done WELL. Be concise and precise."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":532143,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":6842,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":784},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":532143,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6842,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":532143,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0