on first. Product goal: releases are irreversible effects on public registries; the tool must be safe to crash, rerun, run concurrently, and run on a flaky network, without publishing wrong code, tagging the wrong commit, or wedging a release.\n\nRULES: read-only. Do NOT edit/commit/push, do NOT run cargo build/test/publish/clippy, no network publishes. You may read, grep, and run the prebuilt binary /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/15c732d1/tmp/profile-target/release/callisto on scratch repos under a UNIQUE directory `$TMPDIR/adv-recovery-$$` (other agents run in parallel; never use a shared path, never rm outside your own dir). A fake `cargo`/`npm` on PATH inside your scratch dir is fine for exercising release flows locally (see crates/callisto-cli/tests/common/release_harness.rs for how tests do it). Never run git commands in the real repo except read-only `git log/show`.\n\nYOUR LENS: failure, recovery and concurrency semantics. Walk every effect (registry publish, tag create+push, GitHub release draft/upload/publish, release-PR commit) and ask: what if the process dies right before / right after / during it; what if the registry shows the version late, shows a DIFFERENT artifact, rate-limits, or returns 5xx; what if two runs overlap (CI re-run, two merges, local + CI); what if HEAD moves between plan and execute; what if a tag exists remotely but not locally or points elsewhere; what if the registry accepts the publish but the response is lost (non-idempotent effect with unknown outcome); partial multi-package/multi-registry releases and how a rerun adopts them (ADR 3); the E320 version-commit logic (crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/release/version_commit.rs) and the confirmation window / ConfirmationWave (release_execution.rs); fixed-group and dual-ecosystem packages; Python multi-file uploads; npm dist-tag outcomes; wall-clock and timeout handling; receipts. Find states that are unrecoverable, silently wrong, or that wedge a rerun with a misleading error.\nFor each finding give: severity, exact file:line, the concrete interleaving/scenario, whether you REPRODUCED it (command + output) or only READ it, and a one-line fix direction. Rank by severity. Report at most the 12 most important findings; drop speculation that you cannot tie to code. Also list 3-5 things done WELL. Be concise and precise.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c/tasks/a8e92bc1c502c6818.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"10d5f8d8-491b-4598-ad2c-cfbc872079f4","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","branch":"chore/release-target-facts","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"fc2b9e6a-d0de-450a-ab62-75523560c3be","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"chore/release-target-facts","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
