 Product goal: `callisto version` rewrites manifests, lockfiles, changelogs and dependency ranges across ecosystems; a wrong rewrite means a broken or wrongly-versioned public package. It must preserve formatting and never corrupt a manifest.\n\nRULES: read-only on the repo. Do NOT edit/commit/push, do NOT run cargo build/test/publish/clippy, no network. You may read, grep, and run the prebuilt binary /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/15c732d1/tmp/profile-target/release/callisto on scratch repos under a UNIQUE directory `$TMPDIR/adv-version-$$` (other agents run in parallel; never use a shared path, never rm outside your own dir). Use `--no-refresh-lockfiles` where a lockfile refresh would need network. Never run git commands in the real repo except read-only `git log/show`.\n\nYOUR LENS: versioning and manifest-editing correctness. Attack: (1) format-preserving edits in crates/callisto-manifests and crates/callisto-graph/src/apply* (toml_edit, JSON key order/indentation, pyproject, setup.cfg, Cargo.lock/package-lock/pnpm-lock interactions): unusual manifests (comments, inline tables, dotted keys, CRLF, BOM, duplicate keys, workspace inheritance `version.workspace = true`, `[workspace.dependencies]`, `[patch]`, target-specific deps, renamed deps `package = \"x\"`, git/path deps, `publish = false`, npm `workspace:*`/`catalog:`/aliases `npm:`/overrides/peer/optional, PEP 440 specifiers with extras/markers, Poetry vs PEP 621 vs setuptools dynamic versions); (2) semver and PEP 440 handling: prerelease ordering, build metadata, 0.x rules, `none`/`patch` severities, pre mode enter/exit with dependents, snapshot versions; (3) cascade logic (crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade*): cycles, dev-dependency cycles, peer escalation, fixed/linked groups, a dependency range rewritten to one that excludes the new version, the 4n+1 bound; (4) changeset parsing (crates/callisto-model/src/format/changeset): frontmatter edge cases, unicode, huge files, duplicate entries, an entry naming the same package twice, summaries that could inject into generated markdown/PR bodies/workflow outputs; (5) changelog generation and idempotence (running `version` twice, partial failure leaving a half-written tree: is it atomic? see AGENTS.md invariants and callisto_model::atomic).\nFor each finding give: severity, exact file:line, a minimal input that triggers it, whether you REPRODUCED it (command + output) or only READ it, and a one-line fix direction. Rank by severity. Report at most the 12 most important findings; drop speculation you cannot tie to code. Also list 3-5 things done WELL. Be concise and precise.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c/tasks/a4282f58b0b895653.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"10d5f8d8-491b-4598-ad2c-cfbc872079f4","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","branch":"chore/release-target-facts","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7d2a25db-e3ef-4503-9360-a871a0238581","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e