{"parentUuid":"ffd120a9-dfed-4ded-ab37-b5e0df645777","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:WebFetch","toolUseID":"toolu_01P5XxjeKj1XTfV3xejQJBQK","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"tool_complete\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"smoke-main\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"WebFetch\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/gabe/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.1.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-post-tool-use.sh","durationMs":38},"type":"attachment","uuid":"228401ea-ee6b-4baf-bd0f-5e6c98660a6b","timestamp":"2026-10-24T17:44:53.263Z","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"chore/release-target-facts","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
{"parentUuid":"c2640159-fbd2-4e78-b81c-71cbe2706659","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"9060f1dc-711c-48e3-8f57-8ca746997cbc","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WhEYuji8w5ZzX79h36Qxam","type":"tool_result","content":"**What yank does**\n\n`cargo yank` removes a published version from the registry's index, so Cargo stops selecting it by default. Per the page:\n\n- It \"does not delete any data, and the crate will still be available for download via the registry's download link.\"\n- Cargo won't use a yanked version for a new project or a checkout without an existing lockfile. If no compatible versions remain, Cargo returns an error.\n- Yanking does not affect existing lockfiles or direct downloads.\n\nExample from the page: `cargo yank foo@1.0.7`. Yanking requires authentication via `--token` or `cargo login`. Use `--undo` to restore a yanked version to the index.\n\n**What yank does not do**\n\n- It does not delete the crate or its files.\n- It does not stop existing lockfiles or direct downloads from using the version.\n- It does not remove leaked credentials' effects. The page says yanking \"cannot stop further spreading of the leaked credentials.\" For leaked credentials, revoke them immediately.\n- It is not a fix for copyright, licensing, or personal data problems. Contact the registry maintainers for those.\n\n**Re-publishing**\n\nThe page does not say whether a yanked version's number can be reused. It only says the data remains downloadable. Based on general crates.io behavior (not stated on this page), a published version number cannot be overwritten or re-published with different contents, so a fix must be released as a new version.\n\n**Deletion and crates.io policy**\n\nThe page does not describe deletion rules or limits. It says only:\n\n- Yanking should be reserved for \"exceptional circumstances,\" such as an accidental publish, unintentional SemVer breakage, or a significantly broken crate.\n- For security vulnerabilities, RustSec is usually the less disruptive option.\n- A common approach is to publish a semver-compatible fix first, then yank the broken version, so dependents keep compiling.\n- For copyright, licensing, or personal data issues, contact the registry. For crates.io, see its [policies](https://crates.io/policies) or email help@crates.io.\n\nFor exact deletion rules, check the crates.io policies page, since this document doesn't cover them."}]},"uuid":"812b3592-f051-4604-9852-a2289fb71795","timestamp":"2026-10-24T17:44:56.266Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":35598,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"**What yank does**\n\n`cargo yank` removes a published version from the registry's index, so Cargo stops selecting it by default. Per the page:\n\n- It \"does not delete any data, and the crate will still be available for download via the registry's download link.\"\n- Cargo won't use a yanked version for a new project or a checkout without an existing lockfile. If no compatible versions remain, Cargo returns an error.\n- Yanking does not affect existing lockfiles or direct downloads.\n\nExample from the page: `cargo yank foo@1.0.7`. Yanking requires authentication via `--token` or `cargo login`. Use `--undo` to restore a yanked version to the index.\n\n**What yank does not do**\n\n- It does not delete the crate or its files.\n- It does not stop existing lockfiles or direct downloads from using the version.\n- It does not remove leaked credentials' effects. The page says yanking \"cannot stop further spreading of the leaked credentials.\" For leaked credentials, revoke them immediately.\n- It is not a fix for copyright, licensing, or personal data problems. Contact the registry maintainers for those.\n\n**Re-publishing**\n\nThe page does not say whether a yanked version's number can be reused. It only says the data remains downloadable. Based on general crates.io behavior (not stated on this page), a published version number cannot be overwritten or re-published with different contents, so a fix must be released as a new version.\n\n**Deletion and crates.io policy**\n\nThe page does not describe deletion rules or limits. It says only:\n\n- Yanking should be reserved for \"exceptional circumstances,\" such as an accidental publish, unintentional SemVer breakage, or a significantly broken crate.\n- For security vulnerabilities, RustSec is usually the less disruptive option.\n- A common approach is to publish a semver-compatible fix first, then yank the broken version, so dependents keep compiling.\n- For copyright, licensing, or personal data issues, contact the registry. For crates.io, see its [policies](https://crates.io/policies) or email help@crates.io.\n\nFor exact deletion rules, check the crates.io policies page, since this document doesn't cover them.","durationMs":5570,"url":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/commands/cargo-yank.html"},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"c6f9dc99-b041-4010-9c35-e9b9af08cba1","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","branch":"chore/release-target-facts","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c2640159-fbd2-4e78-b81c-71cbe2706659","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"other"},"session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"chore/release-target-facts","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
{"parentUuid":"812b3592-f051-4604-9852-a2289fb71795","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:WebFetch","toolUseID":"toolu_01WhEYuji8w5ZzX79h36Qxam","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"tool_complete\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"smoke-main\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"WebFetch\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/gabe/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.1.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-post-tool-use.sh","durationMs":57},"type":"attachment","uuid":"84c1ee05-665e-42d8-9c11-62655b9d13fe","timestamp":"2026-10-24T17:44:56.265Z","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"chore/release-target-facts","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
{"parentUuid":"a46aaa72-55ce-4fc2-91dd-147f4218c175","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"9060f1dc-711c-48e3-8f57-8ca746997cbc","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ru3VsN6JWRuiQJQHXKyTA2","type":"tool_result","content":"**Unpublishing within 72 hours of publishing:** You can unpublish at any time in that window, as long as no other packages in the public registry depend on yours. The page says \"you can unpublish anytime within the first 72 hours after publishing.\"\n\n**Unpublishing after 72 hours:** You can unpublish if all three conditions hold:\n- No other public registry packages depend on it.\n- It had fewer than 300 downloads in the last week.\n- It has a single owner/maintainer.\n\n**Commands:**\n- One version: `npm unpublish <package_name>@<version>`\n- All versions: `npm unpublish <package_name> --force`, which the page allows only when all versions qualify.\n\n**After unpublishing:**\n- You can't undo an unpublish.\n- A version number that was used can never be reused, even after unpublishing. You must publish a new version.\n- If you unpublish every version of a package, you must wait 24 hours before publishing any new version under that name.\n\n**If your package doesn't qualify:** The page recommends deprecating it instead. Deprecated packages can still be downloaded, but users see a warning you write. Use `npm deprecate <package> \"<message>\"` for the whole package or `npm deprecate <package>@<version> \"<message>\"` for one version. Deprecating the entire package removes it from search results."}]},"uuid":"999919ae-ffd6-4ef0-b5c5-d9dadb989240","timestamp":"2026-10-24T17:44:58.312Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":510373,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"**Unpublishing within 72 hours of publishing:** You can unpublish at any time in that window, as long as no other packages in the public registry depend on yours. The page says \"you can unpublish anytime within the first 72 hours after publishing.\"\n\n**Unpublishing after 72 hours:** You can unpublish if all three conditions hold:\n- No other public registry packages depend on it.\n- It had fewer than 300 downloads in the last week.\n- It has a single owner/maintainer.\n\n**Commands:**\n- One version: `npm unpublish <package_name>@<version>`\n- All versions: `npm unpublish <package_name> --force`, which the page allows only when all versions qualify.\n\n**After unpublishing:**\n- You can't undo an unpublish.\n- A version number that was used can never be reused, even after unpublishing. You must publish a new version.\n- If you unpublish every version of a package, you must wait 24 hours before publishing any new version under that name.\n\n**If your package doesn't qualify:** The page recommends deprecating it instead. Deprecated packages can still be downloaded, but users see a warning you write. Use `npm deprecate <package> \"<message>\"` for the whole package or `npm deprecate <package>@<version> \"<message>\"` for one version. Deprecating the entire package removes it from search results.","durationMs":5652,"url":"https://docs.npmjs.com/policies/unpublish"},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"c6f9dc99-b041-4010-9c35-e9b9af08cba1","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","branch":"chore/release-target-facts","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a46aaa72-55ce-4fc2-91dd-1