{"parentUuid":"31538dc0-485e-4c07-9ea1-06923c78820a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMUj6XcJpd1hJ9LziRpN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1446,"cache_read_input_tokens":607606,"output_tokens":3261,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1761},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1446,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3261,"cache_read_input_tokens":607606,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1446,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1446},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":19958,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"dc1c6ebd-2aab-46bd-9e85-1cf4c62d342b","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgMUj5phoivfXmRbbJnGe","requestRef":"f83ee26b-8dfb-4dce-a9cc-0b44a342c5c3","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"7464bab9-235d-46d0-b041-43b42f6873f9","timestamp":"2026-10-24T17:45:41.983Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"chore/release-target-facts","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
{"parentUuid":"7464bab9-235d-46d0-b041-43b42f6873f9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMUj6XcJpd1hJ9LziRpN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Pulling a published package: what each registry allows\n\nI checked the registries' current docs for this. The crates.io deletion thresholds came from a search summary, not the live policy page, so please confirm them there before we document them.\n\n| Registry | Soft pull | Hard delete | After removal |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **crates.io** | `cargo yank` takes the version out of the index. It stays downloadable, existing lockfiles keep working, and it can be undone with `--undo`. | Owners can delete a crate only within 72 hours of publishing. After that it needs a single owner, fewer than about 500 downloads per month, and no reverse dependencies. Otherwise contact the crates.io team. | A version number can't be republished with different contents. |\n| **npm** | `npm deprecate` keeps the version installable and shows your warning. | Within 72 hours of publishing, if no public package depends on it. After 72 hours it needs no dependents, under 300 downloads a week, and a single owner. | A used version number can never be reused. If every version is removed, there is a 24-hour wait before any new version under that name. |\n| **PyPI** | Yank (PEP 592) hides a version from normal resolution but keeps it downloadable. | Deletion is permanent. PEP 763 would limit deletion to 72 hours after upload; I could not confirm its status. | A filename can't be reused, even after the project is deleted and recreated. Deleting a project also frees its name for anyone else. |\n\n**Delays.** From the cache headers I measured earlier this session:\n- npm serves package documents for up to 5 minutes.\n- The PyPI index and the crates.io sparse index are cached for up to 10 minutes.\n\nSo a pulled or yanked version can keep appearing for several minutes. I haven't measured the delay on any registry's own deletion path.\n\n## What this means for Callisto\n\nI agree with you: Callisto should never delete or yank. Today the `execute` job only publishes, tags and creates releases, so keep it that way. The policy is \"the version is burned, move forward.\"\n\n**The real concern is a rerun after a manual pull.** If someone yanks or unpublishes version X, the manifest still says X, so the next `release` tries to finish X. From the code (not tested live):\n- The registry rejects the publish as already existing, and Callisto classifies that as \"already published.\"\n- The version is no longer visible, so the confirmation waits the full window.\n- The run ends in E157 \"not shown by registry,\" which hides the actual cause and misleads the user.\n\n**Cheap fixes, no new commands:**\n1. **A specific error for this contradiction.** If a publish says \"already exists\" but the registry never shows the version, say: \"version X was published and removed; versions cannot be reused; release a higher version.\" This is small and I'd do it with the other first-release work. First I'd test how a yanked version actually appears to `cargo info` and `npm view`, because I don't know that yet.\n2. **A \"pulling a release\" runbook** in `releasing.md`, covering:\n   - Yank or deprecate rather than delete, since deleting on PyPI frees the name and npm and PyPI never reuse a version.\n   - Publish a fixed higher version through the normal flow.\n   - Leave the git tag alone, because Callisto adopts tags and deleting one invites a re-tag.\n   - Edit the GitHub release notes by hand, and note that immutable releases block asset deletion once published.\n3. **Leaked credentials.** Yanking doesn't help, so the docs should say to rotate the token.\n\n**Why first releases matter most.** Most \"I need to pull this\" cases are a wrong name or bad metadata on a first publish. The 72-hour windows on crates.io and npm exist for exactly that, so the metadata preflight I proposed will prevent a lot of them.\n\n**What I wouldn't build:** a `callisto yank` command, automatic cleanup after a failed run, or any registry write beyond publish. Each adds credential scope and a way to make an irreversible mistake worse.\n\nSources:\n- [cargo yank](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/commands/cargo-yank.html)\n- [npm unpublish policy](https://docs.npmjs.com/policies/unpublish)\n- [TestPyPI help](https://test.pypi.org/help/)\n- [PEP 763](https://peps.python.org/pep-0763/)\n- [crates.io policies](https://www.crates.io/policies)\n- [crates.io development update](https://blog.rust-lang.org/2025/02/05/crates-io-development-update/)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1446,"cache_read_input_tokens":607606,"output_tokens":3261,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1761},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1446,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3261,"cache_read_input_tokens":607606,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1446,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1446},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"dc1c6ebd-2aab-46bd-9e85-1cf4c62d342b","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgMUj5phoivfXmRbbJnGe","requestRef":"f83ee26b-8dfb-4dce-a9cc-0b44a342c5c3","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"767ed6e0-e994-4a86-8a3e-1f8caa00f864","timestamp":"2026-10-24T17:45:47.781Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.c