{"parentUuid":"2693e744-1bd5-42a0-99c2-52a61341816e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"292a1ddc-3040-4aad-8fec-ec43ab952564","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Vcbq6PBrc5koRHGzZte7Z9","type":"tool_result","content":"9:## npm\n13:### Pattern A: manual `.npmrc` via `NPM_TOKEN`\n28:### Pattern B: `actions/setup-node` with `registry-url`\n45:### Choosing a pattern\n54:### Provenance\n60:## Cargo (crates.io)\n73:## Python (PyPI)\n87:### Generated Callisto workflows\n93:### Current Python support limits\n# Publishing: registry authentication\n\nRegistry credential setup only. For the release lifecycle itself (local `callisto release`, generated workflows, recovery, execution semantics), see [`releasing.md`](releasing.md). For the `[registries.<name>]` config schema, see [`config.md`](config.md).\n\nCallisto delegates authentication to `cargo`, `npm`/`pnpm`, and `twine`. Configure credentials for those tools in the publishing job.\n\n---\n\n## npm\n\nTwo supported patterns.\n\n### Pattern A: manual `.npmrc` via `NPM_TOKEN`\n\nSet an `NPM_TOKEN` secret. Add this only in the `execute` job, immediately before the publish step:\n\n```yaml\n- name: Authenticate with npm registry\n  run: npm config set //registry.npmjs.org/:_authToken $NPM_TOKEN\n  env:\n    NPM_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.NPM_TOKEN }}\n\n- run: callisto release execute --intent \"$RUNNER_TEMP/release-intent/release-intent.json\" --receipt \"$RUNNER_TEMP/release-receipt.json\" --orchestration-revision \"$GITHUB_SHA\"\n```\n\n`npm config set` writes the user-level `.npmrc` for later publish calls in the job. The version-PR action receives no token.\n\n### Pattern B: `actions/setup-node` with `registry-url`\n\n`actions/setup-node`, given `registry-url`, writes a project-level `.npmrc` that reads the token from `NODE_AUTH_TOKEN`:","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"0bb95a85-6106-4711-a994-1f30ea2d201a","timestamp":"2026-10-24T17:51:31.359Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"9:## npm\n13:### Pattern A: manual `.npmrc` via `NPM_TOKEN`\n28:### Pattern B: `actions/setup-node` with `registry-url`\n45:### Choosing a pattern\n54:### Provenance\n60:## Cargo (crates.io)\n73:## Python (PyPI)\n87:### Generated Callisto workflows\n93:### Current Python support limits\n# Publishing: registry authentication\n\nRegistry credential setup only. For the release lifecycle itself (local `callisto release`, generated workflows, recovery, execution semantics), see [`releasing.md`](releasing.md). For the `[registries.<name>]` config schema, see [`config.md`](config.md).\n\nCallisto delegates authentication to `cargo`, `npm`/`pnpm`, and `twine`. Configure credentials for those tools in the publishing job.\n\n---\n\n## npm\n\nTwo supported patterns.\n\n### Pattern A: manual `.npmrc` via `NPM_TOKEN`\n\nSet an `NPM_TOKEN` secret. Add this only in the `execute` job, immediately before the publish step:\n\n```yaml\n- name: Authenticate with npm registry\n  run: npm config set //registry.npmjs.org/:_authToken $NPM_TOKEN\n  env:\n    NPM_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.NPM_TOKEN }}\n\n- run: callisto release execute --intent \"$RUNNER_TEMP/release-intent/release-intent.json\" --receipt \"$RUNNER_TEMP/release-receipt.json\" --orchestration-revision \"$GITHUB_SHA\"\n```\n\n`npm config set` writes the user-level `.npmrc` for later publish calls in the job. The version-PR action receives no token.\n\n### Pattern B: `actions/setup-node` with `registry-url`\n\n`actions/setup-node`, given `registry-url`, writes a project-level `.npmrc` that reads the token from `NODE_AUTH_TOKEN`:","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"classifierBoundary":true,"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"13eed2ef-4c57-4164-bb39-4d77c5a9d218","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","branch":"feat/init-defaults","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modifi