{"parentUuid":"fb7136f7-0dc6-4e7a-93f2-42b434769cb7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMVyiUbuJ96GoH1JjsTV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"CI is green. Opening the PR."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":645,"cache_read_input_tokens":676065,"output_tokens":1258,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":645,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1258,"cache_read_input_tokens":676065,"cache_creation_input_tokens":645,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":645},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"c3f13a20-c141-42ed-a159-f18d33fa27c3","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgMVyi7m2A8HdZRHm5Afc","requestRef":"b84360bc-31ea-4f6d-be9e-1d4e6ca7fae7","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"2bd07916-b1c0-44ea-82f4-779d2342e86a","timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:01:47.456Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/init-defaults","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
{"parentUuid":"2bd07916-b1c0-44ea-82f4-779d2342e86a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMVyiUbuJ96GoH1JjsTV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019VX7T56k5WEu3zmE1zcZie","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-501/body_initdefaults_v2.md","content":"Makes `callisto init` work with no questions answered, with sane defaults and the old behavior one flag away.\n\nFound by running `init` on a single crate, an npm and Python monorepo, and a mixed workspace:\n\n- A new user in a script had to pass `--versioning` even for one package, where fixed and independent mean the same thing (E240/E241).\n- Nothing said what to do after `init`.\n\nChanges:\n\n- **Versioning defaults to independent.** A single package is never asked; several packages are still asked in a terminal. `--versioning fixed` keeps the old behavior, and E241 no longer lists `--versioning`.\n- **The release workflow is written by default** for a GitHub `origin` with `--yes`, and the interactive question now defaults to yes. `--no-workflow` opts out. A non-GitHub origin gets no workflow unasked.\n- **A defaulted workflow never fails `init`.** Building it resolves the `callisto@<version>` tag over the network, which would have made `init --yes` fail offline or on an unreleased build. If an unrequested workflow cannot be built (tag unresolved, or the file exists) `init` prints a warning, records it as a diagnostic and still writes the config. An explicit `--workflow` or a yes at the prompt still errors as before.\n- **Next steps** after writing the workflow: the repository secrets for the registries detected (the same list the workflow reads, now one function), `callisto add`, `callisto release --dry-run`, and a link to the first-publish guide.\n- **`docs/publishing.md`** gains \"First publish\" (name, metadata, a token that can create the package, scoped npm access, rehearse with `--dry-run`) and \"Pulling a release\" (soft pull versus delete per registry, versions are never reusable, leave the tag, rotate leaked secrets). The registry rules come from each registry's own documentation, linked there.\n- Specs `CLI-INIT-02`, `CLI-INIT-12` (E240/E241) and `CLI-WF-01`/`02`, and the README quick start, follow.\n\nTests: single package skips versioning and defaults the workflow prompt to yes; `--yes` alone writes the workflow and next steps; an unbuildable defaulted workflow is skipped without failing; a non-GitHub origin writes none. Two integration tests that ran `init --yes` against a GitHub origin now pass `--no-workflow`, because the commit-plan check rejects workflow files by design.\n\nNot in this PR: the first-release preflight (a package name taken by another project currently reads as \"already published\", E320) and the metadata checks. Those are next.\n\n`just ci` passes.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":645,"cache_read_input_tokens":676065,"output_tokens":1258,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":645,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1258,"cache_read_input_tokens":676065,"cache_creation_input_tokens":645,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":645},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_019VX7T56k5WEu3zmE1zcZie":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-501/body_initdefaults_v2.md","content":"Makes `callisto init` work with no questions answered, with sane defaults and the old behavior one flag away.\n\nFound by running `init` on a single crate, an npm and Python monorepo, and a mixed workspace:\n\n- A new user in a script had to pass `--versioning` even for one package, where fixed and independent mean the same thing (E240/E241).\n- Nothing said what to do after `init`.\n\nChanges:\n\n- **Versioning defaults to independent.** A single package is never asked; several packages are still asked in a terminal. `--versioning fixed` keeps the old behavior, and E241 no longer lists `--versioning`.\n- **The release workflow is written by default** for a GitHub `origin` with `--yes`, and the interactive question now defaults to yes. `--no-workflow` opts out. A non-GitHub origin gets no workflow unasked.\n- **A defaulted workflow never fails `init`.** Building it resolves the `callisto@<version>` tag over the network, which would have made `init --yes` fail offline or on an unreleased build. If an unrequested workflow cannot be built (tag unresolved, or the file exists) `init` prints a warning, records it as a diagnostic and still writes the config. An explicit `--workflow` or a yes at the prompt still errors as before.\n- **Next steps** after writing the workflow: the repository secrets for the registries detected (the same list the workflow reads, now one function), `callisto add`, `callisto release --dry-run`, and a link to the first-publish guide.\n- **`docs/publishing.md`** gains \"First publish\" (name, metadata, a token that can create the package, scoped npm access, rehearse with `--dry-run`) and \"Pulling a release\" (soft pull versus delete per registry, versions are never reusable, leave the tag, rotate leaked secrets). The registry rules come from each registry's own documentation, linked there.\n- Specs `CLI-INIT-02`, `CLI-INIT-12` (E240/E241) and `CLI-WF-01`/`02`, and the README quick start, follow.\n\nTests: single package skips versioning and defaults the workflow prompt to yes; `--yes` alone writes the workflow and next steps; an unbuildable defaulted workflow is skipped without failing; a non-GitHub origin writes none. Two integration tests that ran `init --yes` against a GitHub origin now pass `--no-workflow`, because the commit-plan check rejects workflow files by design.\n\nNot in this PR: the first-release preflight (a package name taken by another project currently reads as \"already published\", E320) and the metadata checks. Those are next.\n\n`just ci` passes.\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"c3f13a20-c141-42ed-a159-f18d33fa27c3","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgMVyi7m2A8HdZRHm5Afc","requestRef":"b84360bc-31ea-4f6d-be9e-1d4e6ca7fae7","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"35041594-8f3f-4ab6-8e9e-8e989ecc872f","timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:01:54.372Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/init-defaults","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
