{"parentUuid":"caf37e00-2a3f-4c0f-9a26-0061fe6d470f","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_019KTc8G5B1ug7a4YPUxQQDH","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"tool_complete\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"smoke-main\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Bash\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/gabe/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.1.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-post-tool-use.sh","durationMs":42},"type":"attachment","uuid":"496d0c46-7e69-4088-ba31-b6f0418c5d34","timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:02:42.589Z","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/init-defaults","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
{"parentUuid":"496d0c46-7e69-4088-ba31-b6f0418c5d34","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/tmp/claude-501/body_initdefaults_v2.md","snippet":"7\t\n8\tChanges:\n9\t\n10\t- **Versioning defaults to independent.** A single package is never asked; several packages are still asked in a terminal. `--versioning fixed` keeps the old behavior, and E241 no longer lists `--versioning`.\n11\t- **The release workflow is written by default** for a GitHub `origin` with `--yes`, and the interactive question now defaults to yes. `--no-workflow` opts out. A non-GitHub origin gets no workflow unasked.\n12\t- **A defaulted workflow never fails `init`.** Building it resolves the `callisto@<version>` tag over the network, which would have made `init --yes` fail offline or on an unreleased build. If an unrequested workflow cannot be built (tag unresolved, or the file exists) `init` prints a warning, records it as a diagnostic and still writes the config. An explicit `--workflow` or a yes at the prompt still errors as before.\n13\t- **Next steps** after writing the workflow: the repository secrets for the registries detected (the same list the workflow reads, now one function), `callisto add`, `callisto release --dry-run`, and a link to the first-publish guide.\n14\t- **`docs/publishing.md`** gains \"First publish\" (name, metadata, a token that can create the package, scoped npm access, rehearse with `--dry-run`) and \"Pulling a release\" (soft pull versus delete per registry, versions are never reusable, leave the tag, rotate leaked secrets). The registry rules come from each registry's own documentation, linked there.\n15\t- Specs `CLI-INIT-02`, `CLI-INIT-10` (E240/E241) and `CLI-WF-01`/`02`, and the README quick start, follow.\n16\t\n17\tTests: single package skips versioning and defaults the workflow prompt to yes; `--yes` alone writes the workflow and next steps; an unbuildable defaulted workflow is skipped without failing; a non-GitHub origin writes none. Two integration tests that ran `init --yes` against a GitHub origin now pass `--no-workflow`, because the commit-plan check rejects workflow files by design.\n18\t\n19\tNot in this PR: the first-release preflight (a package name taken by another project currently reads as \"already published\", E320) and the metadata checks. Those are next.\n20\t\n21\t`just ci` passes."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"1dc690b2-253c-40a0-ba3d-0887c9ee51f1","timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:02:42.609Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /tmp/claude-501/body_initdefaults_v2.md changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. Here are the relevant changes (shown with line numbers):\n7\t\n8\tChanges:\n9\t\n10\t- **Versioning defaults to independent.** A single package is never asked; several packages are still asked in a terminal. `--versioning fixed` keeps the old behavior, and E241 no longer lists `--versioning`.\n11\t- **The release workflow is written by default** for a GitHub `origin` with `--yes`, and the interactive question now defaults to yes. `--no-workflow` opts out. A non-GitHub origin gets no workflow unasked.\n12\t- **A defaulted workflow never fails `init`.** Building it resolves the `callisto@<version>` tag over the network, which would have made `init --yes` fail offline or on an unreleased build. If an unrequested workflow cannot be built (tag unresolved, or the file exists) `init` prints a warning, records it as a diagnostic and still writes the config. An explicit `--workflow` or a yes at the prompt still errors as before.\n13\t- **Next steps** after writing the workflow: the repository secrets for the registries detected (the same list the workflow reads, now one function), `callisto add`, `callisto release --dry-run`, and a link to the first-publish guide.\n14\t- **`docs/publishing.md`** gains \"First publish\" (name, metadata, a token that can create the package, scoped npm access, rehearse with `--dry-run`) and \"Pulling a release\" (soft pull versus delete per registry, versions are never reusable, leave the tag, rotate leaked secrets). The registry rules come from each registry's own documentation, linked there.\n15\t- Specs `CLI-INIT-02`, `CLI-INIT-10` (E240/E241) and `CLI-WF-01`/`02`, and the README quick start, follow.\n16\t\n17\tTests: single package skips versioning and defaults the workflow prompt to yes; `--yes` alone writes the workflow and next steps; an unbuildable defaulted workflow is skipped without failing; a non-GitHub origin writes none. Two integration tests that ran `init --yes` against a GitHub origin now pass `--no-workflow`, because the commit-plan check rejects workflow files by design.\n18\t\n19\tNot in this PR: the first-release preflight (a package name taken by another project currently reads as \"already published\", E320) and the metadata checks. Those are next.\n20\t\n21\t`just ci` passes.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/init-defaults","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
