{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","hash":"9f11799d33f441058ecf8f694cbfe9e691b5a4b3747334aac7cae39a48b33314","message":{"role":"system","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Note: /tmp/claude-501/body_initdefaults_v2.md changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. Here are the relevant changes (shown with line numbers):\n7\t\n8\tChanges:\n9\t\n10\t- **Versioning defaults to independent.** A single package is never asked; several packages are still asked in a terminal. `--versioning fixed` keeps the old behavior, and E241 no longer lists `--versioning`.\n11\t- **The release workflow is written by default** for a GitHub `origin` with `--yes`, and the interactive question now defaults to yes. `--no-workflow` opts out. A non-GitHub origin gets no workflow unasked.\n12\t- **A defaulted workflow never fails `init`.** Building it resolves the `callisto@<version>` tag over the network, which would have made `init --yes` fail offline or on an unreleased build. If an unrequested workflow cannot be built (tag unresolved, or the file exists) `init` prints a warning, records it as a diagnostic and still writes the config. An explicit `--workflow` or a yes at the prompt still errors as before.\n13\t- **Next steps** after writing the workflow: the repository secrets for the registries detected (the same list the workflow reads, now one function), `callisto add`, `callisto release --dry-run`, and a link to the first-publish guide.\n14\t- **`docs/publishing.md`** gains \"First publish\" (name, metadata, a token that can create the package, scoped npm access, rehearse with `--dry-run`) and \"Pulling a release\" (soft pull versus delete per registry, versions are never reusable, leave the tag, rotate leaked secrets). The registry rules come from each registry's own documentation, linked there.\n15\t- Specs `CLI-INIT-02`, `CLI-INIT-10` (E240/E241) and `CLI-WF-01`/`02`, and the README quick start, follow.\n16\t\n17\tTests: single package skips versioning and defaults the workflow prompt to yes; `--yes` alone writes the workflow and next steps; an unbuildable defaulted workflow is skipped without failing; a non-GitHub origin writes none. Two integration tests that ran `init --yes` against a GitHub origin now pass `--no-workflow`, because the commit-plan check rejects workflow files by design.\n18\t\n19\tNot in this PR: the first-release preflight (a package name taken by another project currently reads as \"already published\", E320) and the metadata checks. Those are next.\n20\t\n21\t`just ci` passes.\n\n<total_tokens>14943186 tokens left</total_tokens>\n\nConcise output style is active. Be concise: lead with the result, skip preamble and narration, keep only what the user needs."}]}}
{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","id":"3099957f-4cf4-4362-b18f-81deaef75c27","timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:02:42.642Z","version":"2.1.304","querySource":"repl_main_thread:outputStyle:Concise","shapeHash":"761156c7f8e5f9beaaf03c55d45c00e6108ed5cc90a785040747ceaf99aae387","params":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"e79e4252-88ad-4827-b454-1c4d0a401474","keep":1034,"tail":["8313cb4fbee8d4b6fdedbeee06026223694800eb0bc7be68702fd01eb884e64e","2145f99b4c8dacada961f1d627fc8c1d312790992f5894d317c5ac182982e079","9f11799d33f441058ecf8f694cbfe9e691b5a4b3747334aac7cae39a48b33314"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",1036,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"adcc1597cff5128aae521f91044ab80ff7815d3d570199e16b8a5623da0b7546"}
{"parentUuid":"60b3ad82-9a92-4b39-a744-d166f2544526","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMW3t2SPRkuMZHzk1rip","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The `init` defaults are in PR #350, with `just ci` passing, using your two decisions: write the workflow by default, and version independently.\n\n- **Versioning:** it defaults to independent. A single package is never asked, since fixed and independent mean the same there. Several packages are still asked in a terminal, and `--versioning fixed` is still available.\n- **Workflow:** `init --yes` writes it for a GitHub `origin`, and the interactive prompt now defaults to yes. `--no-workflow` opts out, and a non-GitHub origin gets none unasked.\n- **A bug I caught on the way:** a defaulted workflow resolves the `callisto@<version>` tag over the network. That would have made `init --yes` fail offline or on an unreleased build. So an unrequested workflow that can't be built is now skipped with a warning and `init` still succeeds. An explicit `--workflow` still errors.\n- **Next steps:** after writing the workflow, `init` lists the repository secrets for the registries it detected, the first commands to run, and a link to the first-publish guide. The secrets come from the same function the workflow uses, so they can't drift.\n- **Docs:** `publishing.md` has new \"First publish\" and \"Pulling a release\" sections. The facts in the second come from the registries' own pages, which I read earlier. The first-publish guidance on tokens and trusted publishing is my understanding of the registries' behavior, hedged in the text, so please check it.\n- **Specs and tests:** specs and the README are updated, and a changeset is included. Two integration tests that ran `init --yes` against a GitHub origin now pass `--no-workflow`.\n\nNot in #350: the first-release preflight, where a taken package name currently reads as \"already published\" (E320), and the metadata checks. That is the next PR.\n\nRelease PR #349 is open from the earlier merges. I haven't touched it. The remaining queue is the changeset hard-error, skipping non-publishable members, the release-commit allow-list, and the legacy removals. Tell me if you want a different order."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1473,"cache_read_input_tokens":678313,"output_tokens":669,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1473,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":669,"cache_read_input_tokens":678313,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1473,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1473},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"dd049f20-4b79-483a-ad32-3703098b0174","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgMW3sf79MBbAw2FGh7T7","requestRef":"3099957f-4cf4-4362-b18f-81deaef75c27","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"523a4c98-e429-4581-a303-5479b1ec4218","timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:02:48.272Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/init-defaults","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
