e package on every run; a crate with no version no longer aborts every run with E013.\" . 2>&1 | tail -3","description":"Commit, push and open the PR","dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true,"timeout":300000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"fc544b94-86b2-4ed7-9504-454a48e91def","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgMYWCfZzhpvB9k1FdUS6","requestRef":"862eab12-84ba-4ab8-93a1-d5020909d5c5","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"6636ef14-07f4-4e5b-91a7-fc32f7e9cf48","timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:35:02.122Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"fix/unresolved-changeset-entry","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
{"parentUuid":"a43c8799-4f22-4ad8-8fd1-c31ba1be3ad0","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"81e97b21-5b87-4de1-93b0-c0727fa54480","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TJ9jF6izRVG3ge4tqcjaYY","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /tmp/claude-501/body_unresolved_v2.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"da2a94cc-253c-46f7-bd6b-5aaaa811f2c9","timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:35:02.854Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/tmp/claude-501/body_unresolved_v2.md","content":"Fixes two ways a single bad input could break `version` for a whole workspace. Both came out of the adversarial review; the first I reproduced.\n\n**A changeset with one unresolved entry re-bumped its package on every run.** With `\"cargo/core\": minor` and `\"cargo/ghost\": patch` (a typo or a removed package), `version` applied `core`'s minor bump and left the file on disk, because the changeset can't be consumed while an entry is unresolved. The next run bumped `core` again: 1.0.0, 1.1.0, 1.2.0, with a second changelog line each time, and `release` would have published them. Now a changeset with any unresolved entry applies none of its entries and the warning says so (\"none of its entries apply until this entry is fixed or removed\"). It stays on disk, so nothing is lost, and `--strict` still turns the warning into a failure. This matches what the old message already promised (\"will not be consumed until this entry is resolved\").\n\n**A crate with no version aborted every run with E013.** An xtask or other internal tool crate with no `version` (Cargo reads it as 0.0.0 and cannot publish it) failed `status`, `version` and `release` for the whole workspace, even though nothing was releasing it. Discovery now skips such a crate with a note, the same way a private, versionless npm root is already skipped. A crate that inherits its version (`version.workspace = true`) is still a package. Python is left alone on purpose: skipping a dynamic-version `pyproject.toml` could hide the E007 refusal for a co-located Maturin project.\n\nTests: the old aggregate test now asserts the known entry does not bump; a new end-to-end test runs `version` twice through the binary and checks the manifest stays at 1.0.0; a discovery test covers literal, inherited and versionless crates. `VER-AGG-03` and `WS-DISC` are updated, and there is a changeset.\n\n`just ci` passes.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"fc544b94-86b2-4ed7-9504-454a48e91def","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","branch":"fix/unresolved-changeset-entry","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":6,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":1},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a43c8799-4f22-4ad8-8fd1-c31ba1be3ad0","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"fix/unresolved-changeset-entry","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
