{"parentUuid":"3023ec74-b94b-4bf7-8c59-3036bc4a4419","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"81e97b21-5b87-4de1-93b0-c0727fa54480","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015G4cb4e4r3jgQjxTBpWdxq","type":"tool_result","content":"        (\"bare package\", release(&artifact(\"demo\", \"a\", \"ok.tar.gz\"))),\n    ];\n    for (label, body) in cases {\n        fs::write(d.path().join(\"callisto.toml\"), body).unwrap();\n        assert!(load_config_at(d.path()).is_err(), \"{label} must be rejected\");\n    }\n}\n#[test]\nfn invalid_profile_name_or_forge_repository_is_rejected() {\n    assert!(load(\"[release.profiles.\\\"bad/name\\\"]\\nforge-repository=\\\"o/a\\\"\\n\").is_err());\n    assert!(load(\"[release.profiles.production]\\nforge-repository=\\\"not a repo\\\"\\n\").is_err());\n    let d = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\n    fs::write(\n        d.path().join(\"callisto.toml\"),\n        release(&format!(\n            \"forge-repository = \\\"not a repo\\\"\\n{}\",\n        Err(GraphError::InitUnsupportedArtifactBuilder { ecosystem, .. }) if ecosystem == \"npm\"\n    ));\n}\n\n// An existing config is an error, and its [init] table is never read.\n#[test]\nfn existing_config_is_already_initialized() {\n    let dir = workspace();\n    let config = \"[init]\\necosystems = [\\\"cargo\\\"]\\n\";\n    std::fs::write(dir.path().join(\"callisto.toml\"), config).unwrap();\n    let error = detect_in(dir.path()).unwrap_err();\n    assert!(matches!(error, GraphError::InitAlreadyInitialized { .. }), \"{error}\");\n    assert!(error.to_string().contains(\"already initialized\"));\n    assert_eq!(\n        std::fs::read_to_string(dir.path().join(\"callisto.toml\")).unwrap(),\n        config\n    );\n    assert!(crate::config::load(dir.path()).is_ok(), \"[init] still parses\");\n    let permit = ApplyPermit::force_for_tests();\n    assert!(matches!(\n        write(dir.path(), empty_config(), &permit).unwrap_err(),\n        GraphError::InitAlreadyInitialized { .. }\n    ));\n}\n\n/// A write failure during `init` names the exact file it failed to write\n| `[[fixed-group]]` | array of tables | no | Packages that version in lock-step |\n| `[[linked-group]]` | array of tables | no | Packages that share severity, not version |\n| `[init]` | table | no | Deprecated; parsed for compatibility, never read |\n\n## `[changesets]`\n| `product-package` | string | required | Ecosystem-qualified package whose binaries ship as release assets, e.g. `cargo/callisto-cli` |\n| `forge-repository` | string | none | `owner/repo` the product release publishes to |\n| `[[release.artifact]]` | array of tables | `[]` | Declared binary artifacts (see below) |\n| `[release.profiles]` | table | none | Legacy; only `profiles.production` is read, to migrate its `forge-repository` into the top-level key. Conflicting values between the two are a hard error. |\n\n### `[[release.artifact]]`\n\n```\n\n## `[init]`\n\nDeprecated. `ecosystems` (array of strings) is parsed so older config files still load, but nothing reads it.\n\n## Identity and defaults\n\nUnspecified package fields are filled during graph construction: the release trigger defaults to changesets, the changelog to the package directory, and publish targets to those declared by its manifests. Default tags use the display id, so newly created tags become qualified after name promotion; historical bare tags use the ownership fallback described in [identity](architecture/identity.md). Canonical references alone do not repair the open rename/demotion failures.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"8ca2b501-b73f-4713-9335-bf2be9206624","timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:36:38.452Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"        (\"bare package\", release(&artifact(\"demo\", \"a\", \"ok.tar.gz\"))),\n    ];\n    for (label, body) in cases {\n        fs::write(d.path().join(\"callisto.toml\"), body).unwrap();\n        assert!(load_config_at(d.path()).is_err(), \"{label} must be rejected\");\n    }\n}\n#[test]\nfn invalid_profile_name_or_forge_repository_is_rejected() {\n    assert!(load(\"[release.profiles.\\\"bad/name\\\"]\\nforge-repository=\\\"o/a\\\"\\n\").is_err());\n    assert!(load(\"[release.profiles.production]\\nforge-repository=\\\"not a repo\\\"\\n\").is_err());\n    let d = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();\n    fs::write(\n        d.path().join(\"callisto.toml\"),\n        release(&format!(\n            \"forge-repository = \\\"not a repo\\\"\\n{}\",\n        Err(GraphError::InitUnsupportedArtifactBuilder { ecosystem, .. }) if ecosystem == \"npm\"\n    ));\n}\n\n// An existing config is an error, and its [init] table is never read.\n#[test]\nfn existing_config_is_already_initialized() {\n    let dir = workspace();\n    let config = \"[init]\\necosystems = [\\\"cargo\\\"]\\n\";\n    std::fs::write(dir.path().join(\"callisto.toml\"), config).unwrap();\n    let error = detect_in(dir.path()).unwrap_err();\n    assert!(matches!(error, GraphError::InitAlreadyInitialized { .. }), \"{error}\");\n    assert!(error.to_string().contains(\"already initialized\"));\n    assert_eq!(\n        std::fs::read_to_string(dir.path().join(\"callisto.toml\")).unwrap(),\n        config\n    );\n    assert!(crate::config::load(dir.path()).is_ok(), \"[init] still parses\");\n    let permit = ApplyPermit::force_for_tests();\n    assert!(matches!(\n        write(dir.path(), empty_config(), &permit).unwrap_err(),\n        GraphError::InitAlreadyInitialized { .. }\n    ));\n}\n\n/// A write failure during `init` names the exact file it failed to write\n| `[[fixed-group]]` | array of tables | no | Packages that version in lock-step |\n| `[[linked-group]]` | array of tables | no | Packages that share severity, not version |\n| `[init]` | table | no | Deprecated; parsed for compatibility, never read |\n\n## `[changesets]`\n| `product-package` | string | required | Ecosystem-qualified package whose binaries ship as release assets, e.g. `cargo/callisto-cli` |\n| `forge-repository` | string | none | `owner/repo` the product release publishes to |\n| `[[release.artifact]]` | array of tables | `[]` | Declared binary artifacts (see below) |\n| `[release.profiles]` | table | none | Legacy; only `profiles.production` is read, to migrate its `forge-repository` into the top-level key. Conflicting values between the two are a hard error. |\n\n### `[[release.artifact]]`\n\n```\n\n## `[init]`\n\nDeprecated. `ecosystems` (array of strings) is parsed so older config files still load, but nothing reads it.\n\n## Identity and defaults\n\nUnspecified package fields are filled during graph construction: the release trigger defaults to changesets, the changelog to the package directory, and publish targets to those declared by its manifests. Default tags use the display id, so newly created tags become qualified after name promotion; historical bare tags use the ownership fallback described in [identity](architecture/identity.md). Canonical references alone do not repair the open rename/demotion failures.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"a28c8020-9bcd-452a-bb4f-76869cea846d","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","branch":"chore/remove-legacy-surface","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":2,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3023ec74-b94b-4bf7-8c59-3036bc4a4419","permissionDecision":{"deci