{"parentUuid":"a24d7f6e-ea84-4c26-a32b-48f9c9ae1d3e","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Edit","toolUseID":"toolu_012PHJAEfAY3d4QbWHJPmtxB","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"tool_complete\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"smoke-main\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Edit\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/gabe/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.1.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-post-tool-use.sh","durationMs":48},"type":"attachment","uuid":"8e576bd4-1c4e-4735-8dcf-8fdb48363038","timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:36:50.414Z","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"chore/remove-legacy-surface","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
{"parentUuid":"4766ab3c-624e-44f8-bd92-62a25951b88a","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"81e97b21-5b87-4de1-93b0-c0727fa54480","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TNgUsm5xpSBJQtGNZibjZw","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/docs/config.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"7dd75f2d-faac-4c84-8cf9-fca1c489ced5","timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:36:50.494Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/docs/config.md","oldString":"| `[init]` | table | no | Deprecated; parsed for compatibility, never read |\n","newString":"","originalFile":"# Configuration reference\n\nEvery key `callisto.toml` accepts, from `crates/callisto-graph/src/config/{raw,resolve,groups}.rs`. Unknown keys are rejected (`#[serde(deny_unknown_fields)]`).\n\nThis reference describes current keys, not the unimplemented parts of the [polyglot design](architecture/polyglot-v1.md). Every package named in this file must be written `cargo/name`, `npm/@scope/name` or `pypi/name`; a bare name is E317 and the colon form is E316. No release-owner, generic build-input or per-file PyPI configuration exists.\n\n## Top-level tables\n\n| Table | Type | Required | Meaning |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `[changesets]` | table | no | Where changesets live |\n| `[cascade]` | table | no | Dependency-bump cascade policy |\n| `[validation]` | table | no | Status/version validation policy |\n| `[release]` | table | no | Product binary release declaration |\n| `[registries]` | table of tables | no | Registry endpoint overrides |\n| `[[package]]` | array of tables | no | Per-package exact-match overrides |\n| `[[package-set]]` | array of tables | no | Per-package glob-match overrides |\n| `[[fixed-group]]` | array of tables | no | Packages that version in lock-step |\n| `[[linked-group]]` | array of tables | no | Packages that share severity, not version |\n| `[init]` | table | no | Deprecated; parsed for compatibility, never read |\n\n## `[changesets]`\n\n| Key | Type | Default | Meaning |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `dir` | string | `.changeset` | Workspace-root-relative changeset directory. Forward-slash-separated only; rejected if absolute or containing `..` (E116). |\n\nExample: `dir = \".changeset\"`.\n\n## `[cascade]`\n\n| Key | Type | Default | Meaning |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `mode` | string (`\"out-of-range\"` \\| `\"always\"`) | `\"out-of-range\"` | When a dependency bump forces a cascading bump on dependents |\n| `bump-severity` | string (`\"patch\"` \\| `\"minor\"`) | `\"patch\"` | Severity applied to a cascaded bump |\n| `peer-escalation` | bool | `true` | Escalate peer-dependency bumps into the cascade |\n| `preserve-npm-ranges` | bool | `true` | Keep existing npm semver range operators (`^`, `~`) when rewriting dependency versions |\n\nExample (this repo's own `callisto.toml`):\n```toml\n[cascade]\nmode = \"out-of-range\"\nbump-severity = \"patch\"\npeer-escalation = true\npreserve-npm-ranges = true\n```\n\n## `[validation]`\n\n| Key | Type | Default | Meaning |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `allow-empty-changesets` | bool | `false` | Allow `callisto version` to run with zero pending changesets (also settable per-invocation via `--allow-empty-changesets`) |\n\n## `[release]`\n\nCredentials and registry endpoints are deliberately excluded — this table only declares immutable intent slots; execution receives credentials from its caller.\n\n| Key | Type | Default | Meaning |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `product-package` | string | required | Ecosystem-qualified package whose binaries ship as release assets, e.g. `cargo/callisto-cli` |\n| `forge-repository` | string | none | `owner/repo` the product release publishes to |\n| `[[release.artifact]]` | array of tables | `[]` | Declared binary artifacts (see below) |\n| `[release.profiles]` | table | none | Legacy; only `profiles.production` is read, to migrate its `forge-repository` into the top-level key. Conflicting values between the two are a hard error. |\n\n### `[[release.artifact]]`\n\n| Key | Type | Required | Meaning |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `package` | string | yes | Ecosystem-qualified package that builds this artifact (need not be `product-package`) |\n| `target` | string | yes | Opaque target triple — passed through to the builder, never parsed by Callisto |\n| `asset-name` | string | yes | Exact GitHub release asset filename |\n\nExample (this repo's own `callisto.toml`):\n```toml\n[release]\nproduct-package = \"cargo/callisto-cli\"\nforge-repository = \"orin-dx/callisto\"\n\n[[release.artifact]]\npackage = \"cargo/callisto-cli\"\ntarget = \"aarch64-apple-darwin\"\nasset-name = \"callisto-aarch64-apple-darwin.tar.gz\"\n```\n\n## `[registries]`\n\nKeyed by registry name. Three registries are built in, keyed `cratesIo` (kind `cargo`), `npm` (kind `npm`) and `pypi` (kind `pypi`). `cratesIo` and `npm` exist with no URL override even without a `[registries]` table; a `[registries.<built-in>]` entry changes their settings and may leave `kind` out.\n\n| Key | Type | Default | Meaning |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `registries.<name>.kind` | string (`\"cargo\"` \\| `\"npm\"` \\| `\"pypi\"`) | required, except for `cratesIo`, `npm` and `pypi`, which default to their own kind | Registry ecosystem. A custom registry without it fails with E321 |\n| `registries.<name>.url` | string | none | Registry endpoint override. For `pypi` it is the simple index Callisto reads, and the upload endpoint unless `publish-url` is set |\n| `registries.<name>.publish-url` | string | `url` | `pypi` only: the endpoint Twine uploads to when it differs from the index. Same HTTPS rules as `url` |\n| `registries.<name>.publish-timeout` | string | `15m` | The longest one publish command (`cargo publish`, `npm publish`, `twine upload`) may run before Callisto stops it with E025. Same format and range as `confirm-timeout` |\n| `registries.<name>.confirm-timeout` | string | `6m` for `npm` and `pypi`, `2m` for `cargo` | How long Callisto waits for a version it just published to appear on the registry before failing with E157. A whole number with `s`, `m` or `h`, from `1s` to `1h`. npm serves package documents from a cache that can answer stale for up to 5 minutes; raise it for a slower registry, and keep the release job's `timeout-minutes` above it |\n\nFor `pypi`, set `publish-url` when the index and the upload endpoint differ, for example `url = \"https://test.pypi.org/simple\"` with `publish-url = \"https://test.pypi.org/legacy/\"`; see [Python support limits](publishing.md#current-python-support-limits). Accepting `nuget` as a target string does not provide a working NuGet publisher.\n\nExample:\n```toml\n[registries.internal-npm]\nkind = \"npm\"\nurl = \"https://npm.internal.example.com\"\n```\n\n## `[[package]]` and `[[package-set]]`\n\nBoth blocks share five override fields, parsed identically; `[[package]]` also accepts `previous-tag-templates`. `[[package]]`'s `match` is an exact ecosystem-qualified id: the package's own name in that ecosystem, which for a dual package can differ per ecosystem (first matching rule wins). `[[package-set]]`'s `match` is an ecosystem-qualified glob, compared with each package's name in that ecosystem, and can match many packages at once; a rule for several ecosystems is one rule per ecosystem; `[[package]]` always takes priority over `[[package-set]]` for a given package.\n\n| Key | Type | Default | Meaning |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `match` | string | required | `[[package]]`: exact `ecosystem/name`. `[[package-set]]`: `ecosystem/glob`. A name without its ecosystem is E317. |\n| `release-trigger` | string (`\"changeset\"` \\| `\"auto\"`) | none — every field here is an `Option`; omitted means \"use this package's own default\", not a config-level default | What causes this package to be considered for release |\n| `publish-to` | array of strings (`\"crates-io\"` \\| `\"npm\"` \\| `\"pypi\"` \\| `\"nuget\"` \\| `\"github-release\"` \\| `\"none\"`) | none | Where this package publishes |\n| `tag-template` | string | none | Git tag template, e.g. `\"callisto@{version}\"` |\n| `previous-tag-templates` | array of strings | `[]` | `[[package]]` only (`[[package-set]]` rejects it). Earlier tag templates checked (in order) for this package's last release tag, only if `tag-template` finds none. They are matched by name only, so this is how a renamed package claims the tags it made under its old name |\n| `changelog` | string | none | Changelog path, relative to the package's own root. Forward-slash-separated only; rejected if absolute or containing `..` (E113). |\n| `pre-major-inference` | string (`\"off\"` \\| `\"conservative\"` \\| `\"conservative-feat\"`) | `\"off\"` | Pre-1.0 severity-downgrade policy: `conservative` downgrades an inferred Major to Minor; `conservative-feat` also downgrades Minor to Patch |\n\nExample (this repo's own `callisto.toml`):\n```toml\n[[package]]\nmatch = \"cargo/callisto-cli\"\npublish-to = [\"crates-io\", \"github-release\"]\ntag-template = \"callisto@{version}\"\nprevious-tag-templates = [\"callisto-cli@{version}\"]\n```\n\n## `[[fixed-group]]` and `[[linked-group]]`\n\nNeither has a config-level default for its fields — both are required when the block is present.\n\n| Key | Type | Required | Meaning |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `name` | string | yes | Group identifier, unique across both fixed and linked groups |\n| `members` | array of strings | yes, non-empty | `ecosystem/name` of each package in the group. A platform package is named by its native name |\n\n`[[fixed-group]]`: all members bump in lock-step from the group's alignment base. `[[linked-group]]`: every member receives the highest severity and aligns to the highest target version produced by the members' bumps. Both currently require compatible version grammars; neither is an automatic cross-language version converter.\n\nExample (this repo's own `callisto.toml`):\n```toml\n[[fixed-group]]\nname = \"workspace\"\nmembers = [\"cargo/callisto-model\", \"cargo/callisto-manifests\", \"cargo/callisto-graph\", \"cargo/callisto-cli\"]\n```\n\n## `[init]`\n\nDeprecated. `ecosystems` (array of strings) is parsed so older config files still load, but nothing reads it.\n\n## Identity and defaults\n\nUnspecified package fields are filled during graph construction: the release trigger defaults to changesets, the changelog to the package directory, and publish targets to those declared by its manifests. Default tags use the display id, so newly created tags become qualified after name promotion; historical bare tags use the ownership fallback described in [identity](architecture/identity.md). Canonical references alone do not repair the open rename/demotion failures.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":17,"oldLines":7,"newStart":17,"newLines":6,"lines":[" | `[[package-set]]` | array of tables | no | Per-package glob-match overrides |"," | `[[fixed-group]]` | array of tables | no | Packages that version in lock-step |"," | `[[linked-group]]` | array of tables | no | Packages that share severity, not version |","-| `[init]` | table | no | Deprecated; parsed for compatibility, never read |"," "," ## `[changesets]`"," "]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4766ab3c-624e-44f8-bd92-62a25951b88a","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"chore/remove-legacy-surface","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
{"parentUuid":"7dd75f2d-faac-4c84-8cf9-fca1c489ced5","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Edit","toolUseID":"toolu_01TNgUsm5xpSBJQtGNZibjZw","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"tool_complete\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"smoke-main\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Edit\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/gabe/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.1.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-post-tool-use.sh","durationMs":48},"type":"attachment","uuid":"2f25de65-8a0f-49ab-b7f1-2fd6c8f69b5a","timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:36:50.493Z","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"chore/remove-legacy-surface","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
