{"parentUuid":"2bafa94b-7acf-466b-82bf-096f95fa748a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMZMWWEJTrmCxExFRJmg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"CI is green (the `remote origin already exists` line is a test fixture's expected noise). Opening the PR."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1714,"cache_read_input_tokens":765511,"output_tokens":1175,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1714,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1175,"cache_read_input_tokens":765511,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1714,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1714},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"ee33d6f4-147f-4ae4-94dc-fcf48a5d4616","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgMZMVxFMtSwwmJ5QW917","requestRef":"f385ce6e-6657-4b89-9b73-0cac939b8dbe","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"1509df9e-4001-48f5-97ee-7a49914ea590","timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:46:11.729Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"chore/remove-legacy-surface","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
{"parentUuid":"1509df9e-4001-48f5-97ee-7a49914ea590","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMZMWWEJTrmCxExFRJmg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01U2whD47apjsZKpQMBjWERb","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-501/body_legacy_v2.md","content":"Removes surface that would otherwise become a 1.0 promise, and tightens which credentials child processes see. All of it was found dead, deprecated or unsafe in the adversarial review; nothing here is a feature we plan to bring back soon.\n\nRemoved:\n\n- **`[init]` table** in `callisto.toml`: \"deprecated, parsed for compatibility, never read\".\n- **`[release.profiles]` table**: it existed only to migrate `profiles.production.forge-repository` into `[release].forge-repository`. A config that still has either table now fails to load with serde's unknown-key error, which names the key.\n- **`setup_git_user` action input**: a documented no-op. GitHub only warns when a workflow still passes an unknown input.\n- **The installer's `cargo install --git main` fallback.** With `version: latest`, a failed prebuilt download plus a failed crates.io install would build unreleased `main` and run it in a job holding publish credentials. `latest` now fails like a pinned version does. I did not add `--source-ref` to the attestation check, as the review suggested: the release workflow runs on a push to `main`, so pinning the release tag would reject every genuine asset.\n\nTightened:\n\n- `ACTIONS_ID_TOKEN_REQUEST_TOKEN` and `ACTIONS_ID_TOKEN_REQUEST_URL` (the job's OIDC request) now reach only npm, pnpm, yarn and bun, which need them for provenance, and are withheld from cargo, git, gh, twine and the Python build. The token is added to the redacted list, and the credential-matrix tests cover both.\n\nNot changed, on purpose:\n\n- `publish-to = \"nuget\"` is still accepted although there is no publisher; that is a decision for the owner.\n- `CARGO_REGISTRIES_<NAME>_TOKEN` is redacted from output but not removed from other tools' environments. Its name is dynamic, so it needs a pattern-based scrub, not a list entry. Tracked as a follow-up.\n\nTests: the legacy-profile tests are replaced by one asserting the tables are rejected; the setup action's fallback test now asserts `latest` fails without a git install; `just ci` passes. Specs `ERR-03` and the config reference are updated, and there is a changeset.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1714,"cache_read_input_tokens":765511,"output_tokens":1175,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1714,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1175,"cache_read_input_tokens":765511,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1714,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1714},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01U2whD47apjsZKpQMBjWERb":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-501/body_legacy_v2.md","content":"Removes surface that would otherwise become a 1.0 promise, and tightens which credentials child processes see. All of it was found dead, deprecated or unsafe in the adversarial review; nothing here is a feature we plan to bring back soon.\n\nRemoved:\n\n- **`[init]` table** in `callisto.toml`: \"deprecated, parsed for compatibility, never read\".\n- **`[release.profiles]` table**: it existed only to migrate `profiles.production.forge-repository` into `[release].forge-repository`. A config that still has either table now fails to load with serde's unknown-key error, which names the key.\n- **`setup_git_user` action input**: a documented no-op. GitHub only warns when a workflow still passes an unknown input.\n- **The installer's `cargo install --git main` fallback.** With `version: latest`, a failed prebuilt download plus a failed crates.io install would build unreleased `main` and run it in a job holding publish credentials. `latest` now fails like a pinned version does. I did not add `--source-ref` to the attestation check, as the review suggested: the release workflow runs on a push to `main`, so pinning the release tag would reject every genuine asset.\n\nTightened:\n\n- `ACTIONS_ID_TOKEN_REQUEST_TOKEN` and `ACTIONS_ID_TOKEN_REQUEST_URL` (the job's OIDC request) now reach only npm, pnpm, yarn and bun, which need them for provenance, and are withheld from cargo, git, gh, twine and the Python build. The token is added to the redacted list, and the credential-matrix tests cover both.\n\nNot changed, on purpose:\n\n- `publish-to = \"nuget\"` is still accepted although there is no publisher; that is a decision for the owner.\n- `CARGO_REGISTRIES_<NAME>_TOKEN` is redacted from output but not removed from other tools' environments. Its name is dynamic, so it needs a pattern-based scrub, not a list entry. Tracked as a follow-up.\n\nTests: the legacy-profile tests are replaced by one asserting the tables are rejected; the setup action's fallback test now asserts `latest` fails without a git install; `just ci` passes. Specs `ERR-03` and the config reference are updated, and there is a changeset.\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"ee33d6f4-147f-4ae4-94dc-fcf48a5d4616","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgMZMVxFMtSwwmJ5QW917","requestRef":"f385ce6e-6657-4b89-9b73-0cac939b8dbe","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c4fa313f-4af8-4071-988e-b4a99076b97d","timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:46:17.044Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"extern