{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","hash":"7a43f92d63e73cb7cc89d40a224afa0bc30a868811643761fa0c727a3a409ca7","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'll revert my edit to `errors.md` since the help text needs to match it exactly, and instead add the trust-boundary paragraph to `publishing.md` right before the npm section.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01V1cKPN1c4JXfMLUM1nyKX2","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/docs/errors.md","old_string":" does not match what this commit claims to release, or the commit changes a path a version commit may not (anything but manifests, lockfiles, changelogs, changesets and the decision file). Reconcile the commit's contents with its release decision instead of regenerating the intent, and move other edits to a separate commit. |","new_str":" does not match what this commit claims to release. Reconcile the commit's contents with its release decision instead of regenerating the intent. |"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HtJcBmh5UZvgVLmMEvLCBq","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/docs/publishing.md","old_string":"---\n\n## npm\n\nTwo supported patterns.","new_str":"---\n\n## Where a publish goes\n\nA registry with no `url` in `callisto.toml` publishes wherever the checkout's own configuration says: `.npmrc` for npm and `.cargo/config.toml` for Cargo. Callisto honors that on purpose, so a private registry set there keeps working, and it means those files decide where the registry token is sent. Review changes to them like code. A release pull request cannot carry such a change: a version commit may only touch manifests, lockfiles, changelogs, changesets and the decision file, and any other path fails verification with E165. Set `url` on the registry entry to pin the destination in `callisto.toml`.\n\n---\n\n## npm\n\nTwo supported patterns."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MUaQ8pQCvE5yQgB3nWf6i1","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"rm -rf crates/.claude; cargo fmt --all; zsh /tmp/claude-501/ci.sh /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main /tmp/claude-501/ci-allow.log; tail -2 /tmp/claude-501/ci-allow.log; grep -n \" FAILED\\|panicked\\|^error\\|^FAIL\" /tmp/claude-501/ci-allow.log | head -5","description":"Rerun the full CI","dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true,"timeout":3000000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
