{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","id":"0bc3e6e0-7b5b-4bc6-9a49-396310000c5b","timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:55:53.807Z","version":"2.1.304","querySource":"repl_main_thread:outputStyle:Concise","shapeHash":"761156c7f8e5f9beaaf03c55d45c00e6108ed5cc90a785040747ceaf99aae387","params":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"add8f1f0-bac9-4254-be57-535354155305","keep":1253,"tail":["7a43f92d63e73cb7cc89d40a224afa0bc30a868811643761fa0c727a3a409ca7","527304eec68b2598f7aa69ce7949c02bed8f3fe01ab91ab85ea760b7eb075a50","40047ff387396cadab4917ceeb1a0a60e4d4b096091c5d29083403c78ba08d7b"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",1255,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"e1bda05be073a58dc87a6eeed21f3332adae36b09503c29646329e41bdfac2b1"}
{"parentUuid":"87e103c5-ff73-4d37-aac0-cd4e21553f0b","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01V1cKPN1c4JXfMLUM1nyKX2","copy":"wire"},{"id":"toolu_01HtJcBmh5UZvgVLmMEvLCBq","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"a8c990ed-e233-41c6-8d86-b936595bcf3a","timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:56:01.944Z","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"fix/release-commit-allowlist","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
{"type":"file-history-delta","messageId":"1d2e67e4-b931-428e-810b-88bb0b7ffac3","snapshotMessageId":"28445a04-1498-448c-96bc-3f399f0eeb15","trackingPath":"/tmp/claude-501/body_allowlist.md","backup":{"backupFileName":null,"version":1,"backupTime":"2026-10-24T18:56:04.113Z","realParentDir":"/private/tmp/claude-501"},"timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:56:04.114Z"}
{"parentUuid":"a8c990ed-e233-41c6-8d86-b936595bcf3a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMa77f2hq2hzUY87UrdK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SjkNqw6bvm52dTTgTMtYrm","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-501/body_allowlist.md","content":"A release commit is now checked for what else it changes. This closes the gap that the committed decision was only tied to manifests, changelogs and consumed changesets, so a release pull request on the bot's branch could carry any other change (source, `build.rs`, `.npmrc`, `.cargo/config.toml`, `callisto.toml`, an action) and still verify, then run in the credentialed `execute` job.\n\nVerification (E165) now refuses a version commit that touches any path other than:\n\n- a manifest (`Cargo.toml`, `package.json`, `pyproject.toml`) or a lockfile Callisto refreshes (`Cargo.lock`, `package-lock.json`, `npm-shrinkwrap.json`, `pnpm-lock.yaml`, `yarn.lock`, `bun.lock`, `bun.lockb`, `uv.lock`, `poetry.lock`, `pdm.lock`), anywhere in the tree;\n- a package's configured changelog;\n- the decision file;\n- a direct-child changeset, or `pre.json` in the changesets directory.\n\nThe error names the path (`UnexpectedPath`). The path check runs after the existing decision and changeset checks, so those reasons are reported first as before. A path allow-list was enough; re-running `version` on the parent and comparing trees would have been far more machinery for the same protection.\n\n**What this does not change, on purpose.** I also looked at binding built-in registry destinations (always passing `--registry`). I tested npm 11 with a hostile `.npmrc` and `publishConfig.registry`: `--registry` alone still sends a scoped package to the `.npmrc` scope registry, and only adding `--@scope:registry` overrides it. More importantly, Callisto honors the project's `.npmrc` and `.cargo/config.toml` deliberately (a private registry is configured there), so forcing npmjs would publish private packages publicly. The destination of a registry with no `url` therefore stays decided by those files. With this PR a release PR cannot change them, and `publishing.md` has a new \"Where a publish goes\" section that says so and points at `url` for pinning.\n\nA custom `version_command` that edits other files in the same commit will now fail with E165; move those edits to a separate commit. I did not add a configuration key for extra paths: no one has asked, and it can be added without breaking anything.\n\nTests: a set of legitimate extra paths (a nested manifest, a pnpm lockfile, `pre.json`) verifies, and eight others (`build.rs`, `src/lib.rs`, `.npmrc`, `.cargo/config.toml`, `callisto.toml`, an action file, a lookalike `Cargo.toml.bak`, `.changeset/config.json`) are each refused with the path named. `REL` spec and a changeset updated; `just ci` passes.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1431,"cache_read_input_tokens":801381,"output_tokens":1289,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1431,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1289,"cache_read_input_tokens":801381,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1431,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1431},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01SjkNqw6bvm52dTTgTMtYrm":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-501/body_allowlist.md","content":"A release commit is now checked for what else it changes. This closes the gap that the committed decision was only tied to manifests, changelogs and consumed changesets, so a release pull request on the bot's branch could carry any other change (source, `build.rs`, `.npmrc`, `.cargo/config.toml`, `callisto.toml`, an action) and still verify, then run in the credentialed `execute` job.\n\nVerification (E165) now refuses a version commit that touches any path other than:\n\n- a manifest (`Cargo.toml`, `package.json`, `pyproject.toml`) or a lockfile Callisto refreshes (`Cargo.lock`, `package-lock.json`, `npm-shrinkwrap.json`, `pnpm-lock.yaml`, `yarn.lock`, `bun.lock`, `bun.lockb`, `uv.lock`, `poetry.lock`, `pdm.lock`), anywhere in the tree;\n- a package's configured changelog;\n- the decision file;\n- a direct-child changeset, or `pre.json` in the changesets directory.\n\nThe error names the path (`UnexpectedPath`). The path check runs after the existing decision and changeset checks, so those reasons are reported first as before. A path allow-list was enough; re-running `version` on the parent and comparing trees would have been far more machinery for the same protection.\n\n**What this does not change, on purpose.** I also looked at binding built-in registry destinations (always passing `--registry`). I tested npm 11 with a hostile `.npmrc` and `publishConfig.registry`: `--registry` alone still sends a scoped package to the `.npmrc` scope registry, and only adding `--@scope:registry` overrides it. More importantly, Callisto honors the project's `.npmrc` and `.cargo/config.toml` deliberately (a private registry is configured there), so forcing npmjs would publish private packages publicly. The destination of a registry with no `url` therefore stays decided by those files. With this PR a release PR cannot change them, and `publishing.md` has a new \"Where a publish goes\" section that says so and points at `url` for pinning.\n\nA custom `version_command` that edits other files in the same commit will now fail with E165; move those edits to a separate commit. I did not add a configuration key for extra paths: no one has asked, and it can be added without breaking anything.\n\nTests: a set of legitimate extra paths (a nested manifest, a pnpm lockfile, `pre.json`) verifies, and eight others (`build.rs`, `src/lib.rs`, `.npmrc`, `.cargo/config.toml`, `callisto.toml`, an action file, a lookalike `Cargo.toml.bak`, `.changeset/config.json`) are each refused with the path named. `REL` spec and a changeset updated; `just ci` passes.\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"55ec9c7a-57e5-4cf3-b6bf-ed2d62b65a72","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgMa779WdKsmPg4Pa3VnV","requestRef":"0bc3e6e0-7b5b-4bc6-9a49-396310000c5b","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"1d2e67e4-b931-428e-810b-88bb0b7ffac3","timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:56:01.943Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"fix/release-commit-allowlist","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
