{"parentUuid":"24869292-5747-4eda-9927-c636b9bfcf52","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"81e97b21-5b87-4de1-93b0-c0727fa54480","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019EEmjHvJxEc6ZrnxYi26sx","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/docs/specs/release.json has been updated successfully."}]},"uuid":"850098d2-0535-4909-8e2c-271028eab10c","timestamp":"2026-10-24T19:00:25.844Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/docs/specs/release.json","oldString":"or when they match. PyPI is not checked.\"\n    },","newString":"or when they match. PyPI is not checked. When the package has no tag in this repository (a first release) and the registry holds the version under a differing repository, `release` and `release --dry-run` fail with E322 before anything else, because the version is another project's; tagging the commit that set the version by hand makes the package no longer a first release.\"\n    },","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":260,"oldLines":7,"newStart":260,"newLines":7,"lines":["     },","     {","       \"id\": \"REL-PUB-14\",","-      \"criterion\": \"When a Cargo or npm registry publish is adopted because the exact version is already published, and the registry entry names a repository whose host, owner and name differ from the `origin` remote's (compared case-insensitively, ignoring `.git`, `git+` and URL form), Callisto prints a warning on stderr naming both repositories. The run still adopts the version. No warning is printed when the registry names no repository, when either value cannot be read as a repository, or when they match. PyPI is not checked.\"","+      \"criterion\": \"When a Cargo or npm registry publish is adopted because the exact version is already published, and the registry entry names a repository whose host, owner and name differ from the `origin` remote's (compared case-insensitively, ignoring `.git`, `git+` and URL form), Callisto prints a warning on stderr naming both repositories. The run still adopts the version. No warning is printed when the registry names no repository, when either value cannot be read as a repository, or when they match. PyPI is not checked. When the package has no tag in this repository (a first release) and the registry holds the version under a differing repository, `release` and `release --dry-run` fail with E322 before anything else, because the version is another project's; tagging the commit that set the version by hand makes the package no longer a first release.\"","     },","     {","       \"id\": \"REL-PUB-15\","]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"24869292-5747-4eda-9927-c636b9bfcf52","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"fix/taken-name-first-release","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
