{"parentUuid":"f4873cc1-8168-47b4-933a-581d2b2bf331","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMawDGDMqRVypB7iAqWC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Only #353 conflicts, since the other earlier PRs have merged. I'll ship the finished taken-name branch first, then resolve #353."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":359,"cache_read_input_tokens":852223,"output_tokens":1355,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":172},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":359,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1355,"cache_read_input_tokens":852223,"cache_creation_input_tokens":359,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":359},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"656d9a1f-db5e-4189-9413-e4cf1f688a3e","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgMawCV5rbwKtfuFkZSm3","requestRef":"9cafa951-3ef5-4350-b557-2dcfe15b4a9b","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"fd427127-3c8c-4971-b548-e48e1a0aa090","timestamp":"2026-10-24T19:06:49.213Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"fix/taken-name-first-release","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
{"parentUuid":"fd427127-3c8c-4971-b548-e48e1a0aa090","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMawDGDMqRVypB7iAqWC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019EuxagUCo98BFTMoCnn7Sw","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-501/body_takenname.md","content":"A first release of a package whose name another project owns now fails with a clear error instead of a misleading one.\n\nFound by running `init` and `release --dry-run` on a scratch crate named `single`. crates.io already has a `single` 0.1.0 from another project (`CAD97/rust-single`). `release --dry-run` said \"`cargo/single` 0.1.0 is already published, but it differs from <commit>, the commit that set it. Check out <commit> and run `callisto release` again to finish that release.\" That sends a new user to finish a release they never made. With the files unchanged since the version commit, Callisto would instead have adopted the version, printed only a warning, and tagged this commit as the release of someone else's package.\n\nNow, for a package this repository has never tagged, `release` and `release --dry-run` compare the repository the registry records for the version with `origin`. If both can be read and they differ, the run stops with E322 naming both: \"`cargo/single` 0.1.0 is already published, and its registry entry names github.com/cad97/rust-single, not this repository (github.com/example/single)\". The help says to rename the package, or, if the package really is yours (it moved repositories), to tag the commit that set the version by hand, which makes it no longer a first release.\n\nBoundaries, on purpose:\n\n- A package that already has a tag is left alone. Its published versions are its own history, and the adoption warning from before still applies.\n- A registry that records no repository, a repository that cannot be read, an unreachable registry and a missing tool all leave the check unable to tell, so it is skipped and never fails a plan.\n- It runs only through `plan_local_release` (the CLI's `release`). `init`'s preview uses `plan_workspace_release`, which stays offline, so `init` and its tests never touch a registry.\n- PyPI records no repository for this purpose, so it is not checked, as for the adoption warning.\n\nVerified against the real crates.io with the built binary on the `single` scratch repo: before, E320 with the wrong advice; now E322 with the message above. `differing_repositories` is shared with the adoption warning, which keeps its text. There is no end-to-end test for E322 because the test harness's `origin` is a file path, which cannot be read as a repository; the comparison is unit tested, including the cases that must stay silent.\n\nSpec `REL-PUB-14`, `errors.md` (E322, and the count) and a changeset are updated; `just ci` passes.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":359,"cache_read_input_tokens":852223,"output_tokens":1355,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":172},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":359,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1355,"cache_read_input_tokens":852223,"cache_creation_input_tokens":359,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":359},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_019EuxagUCo98BFTMoCnn7Sw":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-501/body_takenname.md","content":"A first release of a package whose name another project owns now fails with a clear error instead of a misleading one.\n\nFound by running `init` and `release --dry-run` on a scratch crate named `single`. crates.io already has a `single` 0.1.0 from another project (`CAD97/rust-single`). `release --dry-run` said \"`cargo/single` 0.1.0 is already published, but it differs from <commit>, the commit that set it. Check out <commit> and run `callisto release` again to finish that release.\" That sends a new user to finish a release they never made. With the files unchanged since the version commit, Callisto would instead have adopted the version, printed only a warning, and tagged this commit as the release of someone else's package.\n\nNow, for a package this repository has never tagged, `release` and `release --dry-run` compare the repository the registry records for the version with `origin`. If both can be read and they differ, the run stops with E322 naming both: \"`cargo/single` 0.1.0 is already published, and its registry entry names github.com/cad97/rust-single, not this repository (github.com/example/single)\". The help says to rename the package, or, if the package really is yours (it moved repositories), to tag the commit that set the version by hand, which makes it no longer a first release.\n\nBoundaries, on purpose:\n\n- A package that already has a tag is left alone. Its published versions are its own history, and the adoption warning from before still applies.\n- A registry that records no repository, a repository that cannot be read, an unreachable registry and a missing tool all leave the check unable to tell, so it is skipped and never fails a plan.\n- It runs only through `plan_local_release` (the CLI's `release`). `init`'s preview uses `plan_workspace_release`, which stays offline, so `init` and its tests never touch a registry.\n- PyPI records no repository for this purpose, so it is not checked, as for the adoption warning.\n\nVerified against the real crates.io with the built binary on the `single` scratch repo: before, E320 with the wrong advice; now E322 with the message above. `differing_repositories` is shared with the adoption warning, which keeps its text. There is no end-to-end test for E322 because the test harness's `origin` is a file path, which cannot be read as a repository; the comparison is unit tested, including the cases that must stay silent.\n\nSpec `REL-PUB-14`, `errors.md` (E322, and the count) and a changeset are updated; `just ci` passes.\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"656d9a1f-db5e-4189-9413-e4cf1f688a3e","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgMawCV5rbwKtfuFkZSm3","requestRef":"9cafa951-3ef5-4350-b557-2dcfe15b4a9b","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"2e2285f1-a4b9-4767-b4de-1165b8b445e0","timestamp":"2026-10-24T19:06:54.732Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"fix/taken-name-first-release","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
