{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","hash":"e3b51be2319296750632f55f277c3139f388c64bc7a8c3fa991854ea49936fa0","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HUmp4txQXRCfebWhczeB35","type":"tool_result","content":"error: recipe `coverage` failed with exit code 101\nexit=101\n11050:error: remote origin already exists.\n12039:test commands::release::local::tests::ignored_files_do_not_block_a_trusted_run ... FAILED\n12045:thread 'commands::release::local::tests::ignored_files_do_not_block_a_trusted_run' (133319261) panicked at crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/release/local.rs:562:68:\n12052:test result: FAILED. 958 passed; 1 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 31.97s\n12054:error: test failed, to rerun pass `-p callisto-graph --lib`","is_error":false},{"type":"text","text":"<command-name>/rename</command-name>\n            <command-message>rename</command-message>\n            <command-args>callisto-hardening</command-args>\n"},{"type":"text","text":"<local-command-stdout>Session renamed to: callisto-hardening</local-command-stdout>\n"},{"type":"text","text":"<system-reminder>\nThe user named this session \"callisto-hardening\". This may indicate the session's focus or intent.\n</system-reminder>"}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","hash":"72e6d4ad8508acf04844355c1d395c7b23699dcb91c244d4c13097a43727152a","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<system-reminder>\nInstruction files were re-read when this session started; these differ from their earlier copies — each replaces its earlier copy, and the instructions preamble above still applies:\n\nContents of /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/AGENTS.md (project instructions, checked into the codebase):\n\n# Agent guide\n\nRules for AI agents working in this repo.\n\n## Crates\n\n| Crate | License | Depends on |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| callisto-model | MIT | none (external: `michi-graph`, MIT) |\n| callisto-manifests | FSL-1.1-MIT | model |\n| callisto-graph | FSL-1.1-MIT | model, manifests |\n| callisto-cli | FSL-1.1-MIT | model, manifests, graph |\n| callisto-fixtures | FSL-1.1-MIT | model (dev-only) |\n\n- `callisto-model` (MIT) must never depend on an FSL crate. It depends on `michi-graph` (MIT, no dependencies of its own) for dependency-graph validation and ordering. `just license-boundary` fails if anything it builds with is FSL.\n- Check with `grep -H \"^license\" crates/*/Cargo.toml` after adding or moving a crate.\n\n## Commands\n\n- Full pipeline: `just ci` (includes the 90% coverage gate). `just test`, `just lint`, `just fmt`.\n- Performance: `just bench` times `status`, `version --dry-run` and `release --dry-run` over generated workspaces and counts the git processes each starts (`CALLISTO_BENCH_SHAPES=1` lists which). A change that adds a git process per package fails review.\n- Scoped iteration: one `cargo test -p <crate>` or `cargo clippy -p <crate> --all-targets -- -D warnings` at a time.\n  - Not `moon run <project>:test`: its per-project fan-out serializes on `target/`'s build lock.\n  - Never run cargo builds in parallel.\n- Changesets: `callisto add --package cargo/callisto-cli:<bump> --summary \"...\"` (non-interactive). Target `callisto-cli`: its changelog is the one users read. One changeset per user-visible topic, written as the changelog entry: what the user sees now, no internal names or mechanism.\n- Never `git checkout -- Cargo.lock` as cleanup. A lockfile diff means investigate, not discard.\n\n## Invariants\n\n1. Safe Rust only: `unsafe_code = \"forbid\"`.\n2. Manifest edits preserve format: `toml_edit` for TOML; JSON keeps key order and fingerprinted indentation. No regex or line edits.\n3. File writes go through `callisto_model::atomic::atomic_write`.\n4. User-facing errors derive `miette::Diagnostic` with a code and a fix.\n5. No emojis in docs or code.\n6. No cargo features in shipped crates; behaviour is chosen at runtime (#143). The dev-only `callisto-model/test-util` feature is the exception.\n7. No `unwrap()` outside tests (`just lint` denies it). An `expect` names the invariant that makes it unreachable.\n\n## Fixing bugs\n\n- Grep for structurally identical code (same algorithm, other file, ecosystem or mode). A sibling with the same defect is in scope now.\n- N copies of one logic: unify to one implementation rather than patching each.\n- A deliberately deferred sibling gets an explicit record: changeset note, tracked follow-up or code comment.\n- A new shared helper migrates every call site in the same change, or the rest are tracked.\n\n## Specs and plans\n\n- Specs (`spec@1`) live in `docs/specs/`, one per area, current behavior only. Change the spec in the same PR as the behavior. No history, rationale or revision notes.\n- This repo's release workflow has no GitHub Environment or reviewer gate and only `execute` gets registry secrets (owner policy, enforced by `.github/tests/verify-release-workflow-policy.sh`). Never add one.\n- Read `ARCHITECTURE.md` and the matching `docs/architecture/` topic before changing behavior in an area.\n- Read `docs/adr/README.md` before changing release flow, Git access, publishing, distribution, platform packages or manifest writes. Reversing an ADR needs a new ADR the owner accepts.\n- Plans (`plan@1`) live in `docs/projects/`. Delete a plan once its work ships.\n- Code never cites specs: no spec IDs, criterion IDs, section numbers or track names in comments, test names or messages. Describe the behavior instead.\n- A requirement the owner didn't state is a judgment call. Get owner confirmation before it gates anything.\n\n## Writing\n\n- Succinct: short sentences, bullets, tables. No backstory, hedging or filler.\n- Never hard-wrap Markdown or PR bodies: one line per paragraph.\n- Code comments: one short line, only for a non-obvious why. Wrap at 120 columns (`rustfmt.toml`). No history (\"used to\", \"previously\"): git records it.\n- No claude.ai session links in commits, PRs or files.\n\nContents of /Users/gabe/.claude/projects/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/memory/MEMORY.md (user's auto-memory, persists across conversations):\n\n# Memory Index\n\n- [Current Work Plan](project_post_0_10_2_plan.md) — .claude/plans/NEXT-WORK.md (local only, never PR it), rewritten 2026-10-23; older plans in .claude/plans/archive/; verify an item against code before treating it as open.\n- [Prove With the Real Tool](feedback_prove_with_the_real_tool.md) — Fake-tool tests and clean compiles hid the 0.10.1 gh credential regression; reproduce auth/release/registry paths with the real tool, test the failing case first, state what is unproven.\n- [Callisto Self-Release Incident — Durable Memory](project_release_self_hosting_incident_2026-09.md) — Claude invented and later misattributed the release approval gate, misunderstood rerun semantics, and repeatedly declared fixes before publication; records non-negotiable policy, verified failures, corrective architecture, and required incident protocol.\n- [Hardcoded Values — Proactive Search Required](feedback_hardcoded_values.md) — User repeatedly frustrated by missed hardcoded values; always include a dedicated pass in any audit or fix session.\n- [Track 0: gix WASI spike — NO-GO verdict](project_track0_wasi_verdict.md) — mmap ENOSYS in WASI blocks all gix object reads; callisto-moon exec-seam must use warpgate_pdk::exec_command.\n- [Publish Pipeline Audit — 38 bugs, fix ordering, semantic coupling map](project_publish_pipeline_audit.md) — Full adversarial audit complete; 5 P0s, 11 P1s, 15+ P2s; three root patterns; phased fix sequence with dependency order.\n- [Parallel Fixing Anti-Pattern](feedback_parallel_fixing.md) — Parallel agents for fixes fail on semantically coupled systems even across different files; use parallel for investigation only.\n- [Validate Each Fix Individually](feedback_validate_each_fix.md) — Run targeted tests after every individual fix; do not batch changes and rely solely on final CI run.\n- Architecture: ARCHITECTURE.md + docs/architecture/ (moved from .claude/semantic-model on 2026-09-25) — read before implementation work.\n- [Canon Pipeline Scope](feedback_canon_pipeline_scope.md) — Skip canon ceremony for targeted bug fixes with RED tests already written; canon auditor loops infinitely on implementation-detail prose.\n- [Workspace Audit 2026-08](project_workspace_audit_2026-08.md) — CLOSED: 8-dimension audit, all critical/high + all 31 medium/low findings re-verified fixed as of 2026-08-27.\n- [Found Code Needs Same Rigor](feedback_found_code_needs_same_rigor.md) — Committing pre-existing uncommitted code after only \"compiles + existing tests pass\" missed a zero-test-coverage regression; found/inherited code needs the same TDD/adversarial rigor as freshly-written code.\n- [Manifest Persist Track](project_manifest_persist_track.md) — Both Spec A (mutate/persist split) and Spec B (write-batching) shipped; the apply_version_plan redundant-open/persist audit finding is fully closed.\n- [Reviewer Must Actually Run Checks](feedback_reviewer_must_actually_run_checks.md) — lambda-reviewer falsely reported clippy clean once; always instruct review agents to run commands for real, not infer results.\n- [Iterate Reviews in Foreground](feedback_iterate_reviews_in_foreground.md) — Background agent notifications were unreliable across a multi-round spec/plan review loop; user called it out twice — run tight revise-review cycles in the foreground.\n- [PR #5 Release Pipeline Hardening](project_pr5_release_pipeline_hardening.md) — Fixed-group max-severity-wins config + no-compounding test, plus SPEC-005 ReleaseEntry.is_prerelease shipped end to end; all CI green.\n- [Track 7: Revwalk Bounding + Git Fixture Hermeticity Gap](project_git_fixture_hermeticity_gap.md) — nextest+global gpgsign causes ~120s hangs across ~13 test files; deferred as its own future track.\n- [Diagnose, Don't Guess, Environment Issues](feedback_diagnose_dont_guess_environment_issues.md) — User rejected an unverified guess (XProtect); always confirm root cause with a falsifiable test before reporting it.\n- [Recover Stale Agent Results After Session Interruption](feedback_recover_stale_agent_results.md) — Read the raw .output JSONL transcript directly when ListAgents/TaskOutput shows \"completed\" but the result looks like a stale mid-flight placeholder, instead of re-dispatching duplicates.\n- [Always Use Plugins](feedback_always_use_plugins.md) — Route PR/commit narration and audits through courier/ranger/etc. plugin agents by default, not freehand, even when I already have full context.\n- [Terse Comments Only](feedback_terse_comments.md) — One short line max, only for non-obvious WHY; stop writing multi-line prose comments in code/config even though CLAUDE.md already says this.\n- [Cargo Slowness Root Cause](project_cargo_slowness_target_pollution.md) — Hours-long builds were a polluted target/debug (1.7M .o files); wipe it, split-debuginfo=off, one invocation shape, no parallel builds; cold build is 31 s.\n- [No Red-Green, Lean Tokens](feedback_no_red_green_lean_tokens.md) — User dropped red-green testing and wants lean token spend; no heavy agent gating loops; CLI product tag callisto@{version} is intentional.\n- [Never Hard-Wrap Prose](feedback_never_hard_wrap_prose.md) — PR descriptions and all Markdown: one line per paragraph, never manual line breaks.\n- [Succinct Written Artifacts](feedback_succinct_written_artifacts.md) — Changesets, PR bodies, docs: short, plain, no AI slop or backstory.\n- [No Session Links](feedback_no_session_links.md) — Never put claude.ai session URLs/Claude-Session trailers in commits or PRs; public repo, private sessions.\n- [Verify Before Recommending](feedback_verify_before_recommending.md) — Check code, callers and sibling repos before presenting any recommendation; audit findings are leads, not conclusions.\n- [No Thin ADRs](feedback_no_thin_adrs.md) — ADRs only for significant decisions, with rejected options, enforcement and revisit triggers; process rules aren't ADRs.\n- [Budget: Lean Pipeline](feedback_budget_lean_pipeline.md) — weekly token budget; leanest pipeline that still catches bugs; no cleanup agents or rework the user has to review.\n- [Use gh stack](feedback_use_gh_stack.md) — stacked PRs must be native GitHub stacks (gh stack link); plain chained PRs get no CI.\n- [Agent Context Briefs](feedback_agent_context_briefs.md) — curated 2-4k token briefs, one agent per PR via SendMessage, small fixes directly; no forks of long sessions.\n- [Local Tracking, Not PRs](feedback_local_tracking_not_prs.md) — Tracking/handoff plans live in .claude/plans/ (git-excluded); never commit or PR them (PR #201 was closed for this).\n- [Worktree Guard Command Shapes](feedback_worktree_guard_commands.md) — worktree-isolated sessions refuse heredocs, compound commands and text naming git; use /usr/bin/git and scripts written with the Write tool.\n- [Check PR Overlap Before Parallel Branches](feedback_check_pr_overlap_before_parallel_branches.md) — run a pairwise merge-tree check on a PR batch, stack the overlapping ones, hold repo-wide refactors, give a merge order.\n- [Measure Value Before Building](feedback_measure_value_before_building.md) — tag hints reverted (#342): gain was noise-level; measure A/B (process counts + wall) and agree it earns its code before opening PRs.\n- [Entire Auto-Push Is Intended](feedback_entire_auto_push_intended.md) — owner wants Entire session/checkpoint pushes to the public origin; never flag or disable it.\n</system-reminder>\n"},{"type":"text","text":"continue the work that was interrupted"}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","hash":"019e42483bb09f44bfc6a6c8012c2a53026239fa395ad34484a01311ef1d37a5","message":{"role":"system","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Bash command sandbox\nBy default, Bash commands run inside an OS-level sandbox (macOS Seatbelt) applied to each command separately, not to the session as a whole; how it is configured in this session is described below.\n\nThe sandbox marks out what this session was given: the directories listed below, the network destinations the task involves, and the credentials the user supplied for it. Treat that as the boundary even where a limit below is not enforced. Commands can reach more than that — credentials and keys elsewhere on this machine, the user's other projects and configuration, sockets that control this machine or other workloads, cloud metadata endpoints — but being reachable does not make them provided; those are the user's, not the task's, unless the user's request calls for them. If the task cannot be finished with what you were given, do what you can and tell the user plainly what is missing instead of finding another way to it; that report is a complete answer.\n\nHow the sandbox is configured in this session:\nFilesystem: {\"read\":{\"denyOnly\":[\"/Users/gabe/.claude/seed-admin\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/bridge-spawn\",\"/private/tmp/claude-501/bash-edit-diff\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/ide\"],\"allowWithinDeny\":[]},\"write\":{\"allowOnly\":[\"/dev/stdout\",\"/dev/stderr\",\"/dev/null\",\"/dev/tty\",\"/dev/dtracehelper\",\"/dev/autofs_nowait\",\"/tmp/claude\",\"/private/tmp/claude\",\"/Users/gabe/.npm/_logs\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/debug\",\".\",\"$TMPDIR\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.git\"],\"denyWithinAllow\":[\"/Users/gabe/.claude/settings.json\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/.claude/settings.json\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/settings.local.json\",\"/Library/Application Support/ClaudeCode/managed-settings.json\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/.claude/settings.local.json\",\"/Library/Application Support/ClaudeCode/managed-settings.d\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/.claude/skills\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/.claude/hooks\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/local\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/.claude/.cc-writes\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/.cc-writes\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/.cc-writes\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/seed-admin\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/daemon\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/bridge-spawn\",\"/private/tmp/claude-501/bash-edit-diff\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/shell-snapshots\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/session-env\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/plugins\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/hooks\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/skills\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/workflows\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/commands\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/agents\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/routines\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/rules\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/output-styles\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/scheduled_tasks.json\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/launch.json\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/CLAUDE.md\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/projects\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/daemon.json\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/policy-limits.json\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/policy-limits.json.signature.json\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/policy-limits.json.signature-iat.json\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/policy-limits.json.stamp.json\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/backups\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/loop.md\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/cowork_plugins\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/dev-mods\",\"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto--claude-worktrees-smoke-main/15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c/tasks\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/mcp-skill-archives\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/mcp-discovery-cache\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/shares\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/todos\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/statsig\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/logs\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/access-audit\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/remote-settings-helper-consent\",\"... and 135 more (truncated for prompt size)\"]}}\n\n - You should always default to running commands within the sandbox. Do NOT attempt to set `dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true` unless:\n  - The user *explicitly* asks you to bypass sandbox\n  - A specific command just failed and you see evidence of sandbox restrictions causing the failure. Note that commands can fail for many reasons unrelated to the sandbox (missing files, wrong arguments, network issues, etc.).\n - Evidence of sandbox-caused failures includes:\n  - \"Operation not permitted\" errors for file/network operations\n  - Access denied to specific paths outside allowed directories\n  - Network connection failures to non-whitelisted hosts\n  - Unix socket connection errors\n - When you see evidence of sandbox-caused failure:\n  - If the `<sandbox_violations>` block names a denied host, re-run the command with that host in its `allowed_domains` (auto mode); otherwise retry with `dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true` directly rather than asking in prose first — the retry itself goes through the permission gate (a user prompt, or the auto-mode classifier when auto mode is active)\n  - Briefly explain what sandbox restriction likely caused the failure. Be sure to mention that the user can use the `/sandbox` command to manage restrictions.\n - A sandbox denial on a credential, a file or a host that the task does not involve is the boundary above at work: tell the user rather than retrying with `dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true`.\n - Treat each command you execute with `dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true` individually. Even if you have recently run a command with this setting, you should default to running future commands within the sandbox.\n - Do not suggest adding sensitive paths like ~/.bashrc, ~/.zshrc, ~/.ssh/*, or credential files to the sandbox allowlist.\n - Network egress goes through a filtering proxy. Attempt requests and read the error rather than predicting whether a host is reachable; denied connections are reported in a `<sandbox_violations>` block explaining the reason. In auto mode, list the hosts a command needs beyond that in its `allowed_domains` — a denied host named in the block goes there on the re-run.\n - If a command fails to bind or listen on a local port with \"Operation not permitted\" (EPERM), local port binding is off in this sandbox. Treat it as the sandbox-caused failure described above, and tell the user that `sandbox.network.allowLocalBinding: true` in their settings (it applies without a restart) allows it without leaving the sandbox.\n - Opening an app, file or URL with `open`, or scripting another app with `osascript`, is blocked inside this sandbox (macOS Launch Services and Apple Events are off) and fails with errors such as -10822 (kLSServerCommunicationErr), -54, -600 or \"LSOpenURLsWithRole() failed\". That failure is the sandbox, not a problem with what you built; do not retry it with `dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true`. Tell the user the sandbox blocked it and give them the exact command to run themselves.\n - For temporary files, always use the `$TMPDIR` environment variable. TMPDIR is automatically set to the correct sandbox-writable directory in sandbox mode. Do NOT use `/tmp` directly - use `$TMPDIR` instead.\n - If a clipboard utility such as `pbcopy`, `xclip`, or `wl-copy` fails inside the sandbox and the user wants the text on their clipboard, put the text in a fenced code block in your response and tell them to run `/copy` (it copies from outside the sandbox; when the picker appears they can select just that block), rather than writing a file for them to copy manually.\n\n# Environment update\n - Additional working directories added:\n  - /Users/gabe/projects/callisto\n\n<total_tokens>15000000 tokens left</total_tokens>\n\nConcise output style is active. Be concise: lead with the result, skip preamble and narration, keep only what the user needs."}]}}
