{"parentUuid":"2276cc09-327c-4ea4-9450-e691d2c32b87","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"bd6ac0ce-389b-4193-aca8-c1bc4969277a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01223PnYPeFaMcK6hZUFtDjv","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//! Many `<rev>:<path>` blobs from one `git cat-file --batch`, so a read costs a line of stdin and not a process.\n2\t\n3\tuse callisto_model::CommandRunner;\n4\t\n5\tuse super::release_decision::{command_malformed_output, command_non_zero_exit};\n6\tuse crate::GraphError;\n7\t\n8\t/// One object's content as reported by `git cat-file --batch`, for a single\n9\t/// requested `<commit>:<path>`.\n10\tpub(crate) enum BatchBlob {\n11\t    /// The path resolved to a blob at the queried commit; this is its raw\n12\t    /// content.\n13\t    Blob(String),\n14\t    /// The path did not exist at the queried commit -- e.g. a package's\n15\t    /// manifest that was only added later, so it has no blob yet at an\n16\t    /// earlier `parent` commit.\n17\t    Missing,\n18\t}\n19\t\n20\t/// Issues exactly one `git cat-file --batch` invocation requesting every\n21\t/// object in `objects` (each `<rev>:<path>`), and returns each result in the\n22\t/// same order as `objects`.\n23\t///\n24\t/// `git cat-file --batch` reads one object identifier per line from stdin\n25\t/// and, for each, writes to stdout either:\n26\t///\n27\t/// ```text\n28\t/// <sha> SP <type> SP <size> LF\n29\t/// <content: exactly `size` bytes> LF\n30\t/// ```\n31\t///\n32\t/// or, if the object doesn't exist:\n33\t///\n34\t/// ```text\n35\t/// <object> SP missing LF\n36\t/// ```\n37\t///\n38\t/// (git also reports `<object> SP ambiguous LF` for a ref that resolves to\n39\t/// more than one object; `<commit>:<path>` syntax should never be\n40\t/// ambiguous, but it's checked for explicitly below rather than silently\n41\t/// falling through to the blob-header parse.)\n42\t///\n43\t/// This lets every canonical manifest's content at one commit be fetched in\n44\t/// a single subprocess round trip instead of one `git show` per manifest.\n45\t///\n46\t/// Parsing here is deliberately defensive rather than permissive: this\n47\t/// feeds [`derive_release_commit_decision`]'s trust-boundary comparison, so\n48\t/// any framing ambiguity -- an unrecognized header shape, a declared `size`\n49\t/// that doesn't fit the remaining output, a missing separator byte right\n50\t/// after the declared content length, a non-`blob` object type, or a\n51\t/// leftover/truncated tail once every requested path has been accounted\n52\t/// for -- fails the whole batch closed rather than guessing. Each expected\n53\t/// response is also matched against its exact requested object string\n54\t/// (rather than a generic \"ends with ` missing`\" pattern), so a manifest\n55\t/// path that happened to contain a space or colon can't be misread as a\n56\t/// different response shape. Silently misattributing one manifest's\n57\t/// content to a different path because an undetected desync shifted every\n58\t/// later offset would be a far worse failure mode than an outright\n59\t/// rejection.\n60\tpub(crate) fn batch_blobs<R: CommandRunner + ?Sized>(\n61\t    runner: &R,\n62\t    root: &std::path::Path,\n63\t    objects: &[String],\n64\t) -> Result<Vec<BatchBlob>, GraphError> {\n65\t    if objects.is_empty() {\n66\t        return Ok(Vec::new());\n67\t    }\n68\t\n69\t    const BATCH_ARGS: [&str; 2] = [\"cat-file\", \"--batch\"];\n70\t\n71\t    let mut stdin = String::new();\n72\t    for object in objects {\n73\t        stdin.push_str(object);\n74\t        stdin.push('\\n');\n75\t    }\n76\t\n77\t    let output = runner.run_with_stdin(\"git\", &BATCH_ARGS, root, stdin.as_bytes())?;\n78\t    if !output.success() {\n79\t        return Err(command_non_zero_exit(\"git\", &BATCH_ARGS, &output));\n80\t    }\n81\t\n82\t    let mut rest = output.stdout.as_str();\n83\t    let mut results = Vec::with_capacity(objects.len());\n84\t    for object in objects {\n85\t        let (header, after_header) = rest.split_once('\\n').ok_or_else(|| {\n86\t            command_malformed_output(\n87\t                \"git\",\n88\t                &BATCH_ARGS,\n89\t                format!(\"truncated response: missing header line for `{object}`\"),\n90\t            )\n91\t        })?;\n92\t\n93\t        if header == format!(\"{object} missing\") {\n94\t            results.push(BatchBlob::Missing);\n95\t            rest = after_header;\n96\t            continue;\n97\t        }\n98\t        if header == format!(\"{object} ambiguous\") {\n99\t            return Err(command_malformed_output(\n100\t                \"git\",\n101\t                &BATCH_ARGS,\n102\t                format!(\"object `{object}` is ambiguous\"),\n103\t            ));\n104\t        }\n105\t\n106\t        let mut fields = header.split(' ');\n107\t        let sha = fields.next().ok_or_else(|| {\n108\t            command_malformed_output(\n109\t                \"git\",\n110\t                &BATCH_ARGS,\n111\t                format!(\"header for `{object}` is missing its sha field: `{header}`\"),\n112\t            )\n113\t        })?;\n114\t        let object_type = fields.next().ok_or_else(|| {\n115\t            command_malformed_output(\n116\t                \"git\",\n117\t                &BATCH_ARGS,\n118\t                format!(\"header for `{object}` is missing its type field: `{header}`\"),\n119\t            )\n120\t        })?;\n121\t        let size_field = fields.next().ok_or_else(|| {\n122\t            command_malformed_output(\n123\t                \"git\",\n124\t                &BATCH_ARGS,\n125\t                format!(\"header for `{object}` is missing its size field: `{header}`\"),\n126\t            )\n127\t        })?;\n128\t        if fields.next().is_some() {\n129\t            // A well-formed header has exactly three space-separated\n130\t            // fields; anything else is not a shape this parser understands.\n131\t            return Err(command_malformed_output(\n132\t                \"git\",\n133\t                &BATCH_ARGS,\n134\t                format!(\"header for `{object}` has more than three fields: `{header}`\"),\n135\t            ));\n136\t        }\n137\t        if sha.is_empty() || !sha.chars().all(|c| c.is_ascii_hexdigit()) {\n138\t            return Err(command_malformed_output(\n139\t                \"git\",\n140\t                &BATCH_ARGS,\n141\t                format!(\"header for `{object}` reports a non-hex sha: `{sha}`\"),\n142\t            ));\n143\t        }\n144\t        if object_type != \"blob\" {\n145\t            // Every path requested here is a canonical manifest file, so a\n146\t            // resolved object must be a blob; a tree/commit/tag response\n147\t            // means the path resolved to something else entirely.\n148\t            return Err(command_malformed_output(\n149\t                \"git\",\n150\t                &BATCH_ARGS,\n151\t                format!(\"object `{object}` resolved to a `{object_type}`, not a blob\"),\n152\t            ));\n153\t        }\n154\t        let size: usize = size_field.parse().map_err(|parse_error| {\n155\t            command_malformed_output(\n156\t                \"git\",\n157\t                &BATCH_ARGS,\n158\t                format!(\"header for `{object}` has a non-numeric size `{size_field}`: {parse_error}\"),\n159\t            )\n160\t        })?;\n161\t\n162\t        if size > after_header.len() {\n163\t            return Err(command_malformed_output(\n164\t                \"git\",\n165\t                &BATCH_ARGS,\n166\t                format!(\"object `{object}` declares size {size}, exceeding the remaining response\"),\n167\t            ));\n168\t        }\n169\t        // `.get(..size)` (byte-indexed) rather than raw slicing: if `size`\n170\t        // doesn't land on a UTF-8 char boundary this fails closed instead\n171\t        // of panicking.\n172\t        let content = after_header.get(..size).ok_or_else(|| {\n173\t            command_malformed_output(\n174\t                \"git\",\n175\t                &BATCH_ARGS,\n176\t                format!(\"object `{object}` declares size {size} that does not land on a UTF-8 boundary\"),\n177\t            )\n178\t        })?;\n179\t        let remainder = &after_header[size..];\n180\t        // The protocol always emits exactly one LF right after the\n181\t        // content, separate from the content itself. Requiring it here\n182\t        // catches a desynced `size` (from an earlier, unexpectedly\n183\t        // reencoded entry) as an explicit error instead of silently\n184\t        // parsing the wrong bytes as this entry's content.\n185\t        if remainder.as_bytes().first() != Some(&b'\\n') {\n186\t            return Err(command_malformed_output(\n187\t                \"git\",\n188\t                &BATCH_ARGS,\n189\t                format!(\"object `{object}` content is not followed by the expected newline separator\"),\n190\t            ));\n191\t        }\n192\t        results.push(BatchBlob::Blob(content.to_string()));\n193\t        rest = &remainder[1..];\n194\t    }\n195\t\n196\t    if !rest.is_empty() {\n197\t        // More output than the requested objects account for -- either an\n198\t        // extra unexpected reply or a framing desync earlier in the\n199\t        // stream. Either way, fail closed rather than ignore it.\n200\t        return Err(command_malformed_output(\n201\t            \"git\",\n202\t            &BATCH_ARGS,\n203\t            \"response contained more data than the requested objects account for\",\n204\t        ));\n205\t    }\n206\t\n207\t    Ok(results)\n208\t}\n209\t"}]},"uuid":"a5ddd419-713a-4a9c-aa65-860a013678a2","timestamp":"2026-10-24T21:45:17.310Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/git_batch.rs","content":"//! Many `<rev>:<path>` blobs from one `git cat-file --batch`, so a read costs a line of stdin and not a process.\n\nuse callisto_model::CommandRunner;\n\nuse super::release_decision::{command_malformed_output, command_non_zero_exit};\nuse crate::GraphError;\n\n/// One object's content as reported by `git cat-file --batch`, for a single\n/// requested `<commit>:<path>`.\npub(crate) enum BatchBlob {\n    /// The path resolved to a blob at the queried commit; this is its raw\n    /// content.\n    Blob(String),\n    /// The path did not exist at the queried commit -- e.g. a package's\n    /// manifest that was only added later, so it has no blob yet at an\n    /// earlier `parent` commit.\n    Missing,\n}\n\n/// Issues exactly one `git cat-file --batch` invocation requesting every\n/// object in `objects` (each `<rev>:<path>`), and returns each result in the\n/// same order as `objects`.\n///\n/// `git cat-file --batch` reads one object identifier per line from stdin\n/// and, for each, writes to stdout either:\n///\n/// ```text\n/// <sha> SP <type> SP <size> LF\n/// <content: exactly `size` bytes> LF\n/// ```\n///\n/// or, if the object doesn't exist:\n///\n/// ```text\n/// <object> SP missing LF\n/// ```\n///\n/// (git also reports `<object> SP ambiguous LF` for a ref that resolves to\n/// more than one object; `<commit>:<path>` syntax should never be\n/// ambiguous, but it's checked for explicitly below rather than silently\n/// falling through to the blob-header parse.)\n///\n/// This lets every canonical manifest's content at one commit be fetched in\n/// a single subprocess round trip instead of one `git show` per manifest.\n///\n/// Parsing here is deliberately defensive rather than permissive: this\n/// feeds [`derive_release_commit_decision`]'s trust-boundary comparison, so\n/// any framing ambiguity -- an unrecognized header shape, a declared `size`\n/// that doesn't fit the remaining output, a missing separator byte right\n/// after the declared content length, a non-`blob` object type, or a\n/// leftover/truncated tail once every requested path has been accounted\n/// for -- fails the whole batch closed rather than guessing. Each expected\n/// response is also matched against its exact requested object string\n/// (rather than a generic \"ends with ` missing`\" pattern), so a manifest\n/// path that happened to contain a space or colon can't be misread as a\n/// different response shape. Silently misattributing one manifest's\n/// content to a different path because an undetected desync shifted every\n/// later offset would be a far worse failure mode than an outright\n/// rejection.\npub(crate) fn batch_blobs<R: CommandRunner + ?Sized>(\n    runner: &R,\n    root: &std::path::Path,\n    objects: &[String],\n) -> Result<Vec<BatchBlob>, GraphError> {\n    if objects.is_empty() {\n        return Ok(Vec::new());\n    }\n\n    const BATCH_ARGS: [&str; 2] = [\"cat-file\", \"--batch\"];\n\n    let mut stdin = String::new();\n    for object in objects {\n        stdin.push_str(object);\n        stdin.push('\\n');\n    }\n\n    let output = runner.run_with_stdin(\"git\", &BATCH_ARGS, root, stdin.as_bytes())?;\n    if !output.success() {\n        return Err(command_non_zero_exit(\"git\", &BATCH_ARGS, &output));\n    }\n\n    let mut rest = output.stdout.as_str();\n    let mut results = Vec::with_capacity(objects.len());\n    for object in objects {\n        let (header, after_header) = rest.split_once('\\n').ok_or_else(|| {\n            command_malformed_output(\n                \"git\",\n                &BATCH_ARGS,\n                format!(\"truncated response: missing header line for `{object}`\"),\n            )\n        })?;\n\n        if header == format!(\"{object} missing\") {\n            results.push(BatchBlob::Missing);\n            rest = after_header;\n            continue;\n        }\n        if header == format!(\"{object} ambiguous\") {\n            return Err(command_malformed_output(\n                \"git\",\n                &BATCH_ARGS,\n                format!(\"object `{object}` is ambiguous\"),\n            ));\n        }\n\n        let mut fields = header.split(' ');\n        let sha = fields.next().ok_or_else(|| {\n            command_malformed_output(\n                \"git\",\n                &BATCH_ARGS,\n                format!(\"header for `{object}` is missing its sha field: `{header}`\"),\n            )\n        })?;\n        let object_type = fields.next().ok_or_else(|| {\n            command_malformed_output(\n                \"git\",\n                &BATCH_ARGS,\n                format!(\"header for `{object}` is missing its type field: `{header}`\"),\n            )\n        })?;\n        let size_field = fields.next().ok_or_else(|| {\n            command_malformed_output(\n                \"git\",\n                &BATCH_ARGS,\n                format!(\"header for `{object}` is missing its size field: `{header}`\"),\n            )\n        })?;\n        if fields.next().is_some() {\n            // A well-formed header has exactly three space-separated\n            // fields; anything else is not a shape this parser understands.\n            return Err(command_malformed_output(\n                \"git\",\n                &BATCH_ARGS,\n                format!(\"header for `{object}` has more than three fields: `{header}`\"),\n            ));\n        }\n        if sha.is_empty() || !sha.chars().all(|c| c.is_ascii_hexdigit()) {\n            return Err(command_malformed_output(\n                \"git\",\n                &BATCH_ARGS,\n                format!(\"header for `{object}` reports a non-hex sha: `{sha}`\"),\n            ));\n        }\n        if object_type != \"blob\" {\n            // Every path requested here is a canonical manifest file, so a\n            // resolved object must be a blob; a tree/commit/tag response\n            // means the path resolved to something else entirely.\n            return Err(command_malformed_output(\n                \"git\",\n                &BATCH_ARGS,\n                format!(\"object `{object}` resolved to a `{object_type}`, not a blob\"),\n            ));\n        }\n        let size: usize = size_field.parse().map_err(|parse_error| {\n            command_malformed_output(\n                \"git\",\n                &BATCH_ARGS,\n                format!(\"header for `{object}` has a non-numeric size `{size_field}`: {parse_error}\"),\n            )\n        })?;\n\n        if size > after_header.len() {\n            return Err(command_malformed_output(\n                \"git\",\n                &BATCH_ARGS,\n                format!(\"object `{object}` declares size {size}, exceeding the remaining response\"),\n            ));\n        }\n        // `.get(..size)` (byte-indexed) rather than raw slicing: if `size`\n        // doesn't land on a UTF-8 char boundary this fails closed instead\n        // of panicking.\n        let content = after_header.get(..size).ok_or_else(|| {\n            command_malformed_output(\n                \"git\",\n                &BATCH_ARGS,\n                format!(\"object `{object}` declares size {size} that does not land on a UTF-8 boundary\"),\n            )\n        })?;\n        let remainder = &after_header[size..];\n        // The protocol always emits exactly one LF right after the\n        // content, separate from the content itself. Requiring it here\n        // catches a desynced `size` (from an earlier, unexpectedly\n        // reencoded entry) as an explicit error instead of silently\n        // parsing the wrong bytes as this entry's content.\n        if remainder.as_bytes().first() != Some(&b'\\n') {\n            return Err(command_malformed_output(\n                \"git\",\n                &BATCH_ARGS,\n                format!(\"object `{object}` content is not followed by the expected newline separator\"),\n            ));\n        }\n        results.push(BatchBlob::Blob(content.to_string()));\n        rest = &remainder[1..];\n    }\n\n    if !rest.is_empty() {\n        // More output than the requested objects account for -- either an\n        // extra unexpected reply or a framing desync earlier in the\n        // stream. Either way, fail closed rather than ignore it.\n        return Err(command_malformed_output(\n            \"git\",\n            &BATCH_ARGS,\n            \"response contained more data than the requested objects account for\",\n        ));\n    }\n\n    Ok(results)\n}\n","numLines":209,"startLine":1,"totalLines":209}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2276cc09-327c-4ea4-9450-e691d2c32b87","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"ci/hardening-cheap","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
