{"type":"file-history-delta","messageId":"9f3fd3e3-0f67-4401-8dde-0eb396aec09e","snapshotMessageId":"4da908e0-74ed-411c-bc90-0d9bae24cc71","trackingPath":"/tmp/claude-501/body_localtag.md","backup":{"backupFileName":null,"version":1,"backupTime":"2026-10-24T21:58:13.846Z","realParentDir":"/private/tmp/claude-501"},"timestamp":"2026-10-24T21:58:13.847Z"}
{"parentUuid":"83a5a6d8-1bfe-4ce5-acfb-d5d9ddac60de","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMozmgD6HgvGyLdnjsno","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UiJG6xCiKkU9wzSb9UtYBv","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-501/body_localtag.md","content":"A release that tagged locally and then failed to push used to vanish: on the next commit `release` printed \"Nothing to release.\" because the tagged version counts as finished, and the remote tag and the GitHub release never happened. The adversarial review reproduced this, and `releasing.md` already documented the limit.\n\n`release` and `release --dry-run` now run one `git ls-remote` for every package's last tag and warn on stderr for each that exists here but not on `origin`:\n\n> warning: tag `core-crate@0.2.0` exists here but not on `origin`, so its release may not have finished: check out the tagged commit and run `callisto release` again, or push the tag if the release is complete\n\nIt is a warning only. It does not change the plan or the exit status, so nothing that works today starts failing. It prints nothing when there is no `origin`, no tag, or the remote cannot be read. Making the full resume automatic (treating a tag as settled only once the remote has it) is a larger change to what counts as released, and I left it for when someone hits the warning and asks for it.\n\nTest: a real repository with a local-only annotated tag warns; once the fake remote holds the tag in the shape `ls-remote` reports an annotated tag, the warning is gone. `REL-RERUN-08` and a changeset are added; `just ci` passes.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1561,"cache_read_input_tokens":923629,"output_tokens":781,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1561,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":781,"cache_read_input_tokens":923629,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1561,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1561},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01UiJG6xCiKkU9wzSb9UtYBv":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-501/body_localtag.md","content":"A release that tagged locally and then failed to push used to vanish: on the next commit `release` printed \"Nothing to release.\" because the tagged version counts as finished, and the remote tag and the GitHub release never happened. The adversarial review reproduced this, and `releasing.md` already documented the limit.\n\n`release` and `release --dry-run` now run one `git ls-remote` for every package's last tag and warn on stderr for each that exists here but not on `origin`:\n\n> warning: tag `core-crate@0.2.0` exists here but not on `origin`, so its release may not have finished: check out the tagged commit and run `callisto release` again, or push the tag if the release is complete\n\nIt is a warning only. It does not change the plan or the exit status, so nothing that works today starts failing. It prints nothing when there is no `origin`, no tag, or the remote cannot be read. Making the full resume automatic (treating a tag as settled only once the remote has it) is a larger change to what counts as released, and I left it for when someone hits the warning and asks for it.\n\nTest: a real repository with a local-only annotated tag warns; once the fake remote holds the tag in the shape `ls-remote` reports an annotated tag, the warning is gone. `REL-RERUN-08` and a changeset are added; `just ci` passes.\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"b8e7c293-466b-455b-b555-7453c0b14541","apiBlock