{"parentUuid":"9f3fd3e3-0f67-4401-8dde-0eb396aec09e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"bd6ac0ce-389b-4193-aca8-c1bc4969277a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UiJG6xCiKkU9wzSb9UtYBv","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /tmp/claude-501/body_localtag.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"033d0962-aee0-4a25-ab0e-3a92562b82da","timestamp":"2026-10-24T21:58:13.900Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/tmp/claude-501/body_localtag.md","content":"A release that tagged locally and then failed to push used to vanish: on the next commit `release` printed \"Nothing to release.\" because the tagged version counts as finished, and the remote tag and the GitHub release never happened. The adversarial review reproduced this, and `releasing.md` already documented the limit.\n\n`release` and `release --dry-run` now run one `git ls-remote` for every package's last tag and warn on stderr for each that exists here but not on `origin`:\n\n> warning: tag `core-crate@0.2.0` exists here but not on `origin`, so its release may not have finished: check out the tagged commit and run `callisto release` again, or push the tag if the release is complete\n\nIt is a warning only. It does not change the plan or the exit status, so nothing that works today starts failing. It prints nothing when there is no `origin`, no tag, or the remote cannot be read. Making the full resume automatic (treating a tag as settled only once the remote has it) is a larger change to what counts as released, and I left it for when someone hits the warning and asks for it.\n\nTest: a real repository with a local-only annotated tag warns; once the fake remote holds the tag in the shape `ls-remote` reports an annotated tag, the warning is gone. `REL-RERUN-08` and a changeset are added; `just ci` passes.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"b8e7c293-466b-455b-b555-7453c0b14541","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","branch":"fix/warn-local-only-tag","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":6,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":1},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9f3fd3e3-0f67-4401-8dde-0eb396aec09e","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"fix/warn-local-only-tag","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
