{"parentUuid":"473925b7-6744-40f6-bf6e-2eab109a6da5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMp4Wx3Msz8A65WkUm2s","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2986,"cache_read_input_tokens":926183,"output_tokens":1855,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":864},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2986,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1855,"cache_read_input_tokens":926183,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2986,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2986},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":6840,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"ff3dbb4e-f0f5-4b28-9071-3e2c79ca7714","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgMp4WVW2yGeY3XuKDFy8","requestRef":"581aa0de-2be0-4474-9eef-5448ed2883f8","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"71d31b75-be9a-417a-8ae6-7623b7aab9b5","timestamp":"2026-10-24T21:59:02.202Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"docs/stability","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
{"parentUuid":"71d31b75-be9a-417a-8ae6-7623b7aab9b5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMp4Wx3Msz8A65WkUm2s","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QedhjP6V61WpNoPENb7YF1","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/docs/stability.md","content":"# Stability\n\nWhat Callisto promises to keep working from 1.0, and what it does not. A breaking change to anything in the first table needs a major version.\n\n## Stable\n\n| Surface | The promise |\n| --- | --- |\n| The eight commands (`add`, `status`, `version`, `pre`, `snapshot`, `init`, `release`, `completions`) and their flags | A flag keeps its meaning; a new flag never changes what the command did without it. |\n| Exit codes | `0` success, `1` failure, `2` usage error. |\n| `--format json` reports | Every report carries `schemaVersion`. Within a version a field is not removed, renamed or retyped; fields may be added. A shape change bumps the version. |\n| `callisto.toml` | A key keeps its meaning. Unknown keys are an error, so a new key arrives in a minor release and never changes an existing file's behavior. |\n| Changesets | The `.changeset/*.md` format and `pre.json` stay compatible with `@changesets/cli` for npm names; other ecosystems use `ecosystem/name` keys. |\n| Error codes | A code keeps naming the same condition and is never reused. New codes may appear. |\n| Tag names | `{name}@{version}` by default, `ecosystem/name@{version}` once another ecosystem has a package of that name. Pin a name with `tag-template` if a stable tag matters to your tooling. |\n| The GitHub Actions | The inputs of `callisto-action` and `setup-callisto`. The floating `v1` tag moves only on stable releases; pin a commit for a fixed version. |\n\n## CI plumbing\n\nThe generated workflows use `release plan`, `release execute`, `release artifact-manifest`, `release build-python`, `release-pr`, `matrix`, `compose-pr-body` and `schema`. They are hidden from `--help` and work only with the same Callisto version that generated them: the intent, decision, receipt and run envelope carry versions, and a reader rejects any other. Keep the action and the binary on one version, and regenerate with `callisto init` after an upgrade.\n\n## Not covered\n\n- Text output, stderr, warnings and the wording of error messages.\n- The library crates (`callisto-model`, `-manifests`, `-graph`). They are internal and version in lockstep with the CLI.\n- The order of keys in JSON output, and timing or performance.\n- Platforms without a published binary. Windows is not supported.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2986,"cache_read_input_tokens":926183,"output_tokens":1855,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":864},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2986,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1855,"cache_read_input_tokens":926183,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2986,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2986},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01QedhjP6V61WpNoPENb7YF1":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/docs/stability.md","content":"# Stability\n\nWhat Callisto promises to keep working from 1.0, and what it does not. A breaking change to anything in the first table needs a major version.\n\n## Stable\n\n| Surface | The promise |\n| --- | --- |\n| The eight commands (`add`, `status`, `version`, `pre`, `snapshot`, `init`, `release`, `completions`) and their flags | A flag keeps its meaning; a new flag never changes what the command did without it. |\n| Exit codes | `0` success, `1` failure, `2` usage error. |\n| `--format json` reports | Every report carries `schemaVersion`. Within a version a field is not removed, renamed or retyped; fields may be added. A shape change bumps the version. |\n| `callisto.toml` | A key keeps its meaning. Unknown keys are an error, so a new key arrives in a minor release and never changes an existing file's behavior. |\n| Changesets | The `.changeset/*.md` format and `pre.json` stay compatible with `@changesets/cli` for npm names; other ecosystems use `ecosystem/name` keys. |\n| Error codes | A code keeps naming the same condition and is never reused. New codes may appear. |\n| Tag names | `{name}@{version}` by default, `ecosystem/name@{version}` once another ecosystem has a package of that name. Pin a name with `tag-template` if a stable tag matters to your tooling. |\n| The GitHub Actions | The inputs of `callisto-action` and `setup-callisto`. The floating `v1` tag moves only on stable releases; pin a commit for a fixed version. |\n\n## CI plumbing\n\nThe generated workflows use `release plan`, `release execute`, `release artifact-manifest`, `release build-python`, `release-pr`, `matrix`, `compose-pr-body` and `schema`. They are hidden from `--help` and work only with the same Callisto version that generated them: the intent, decision, receipt and run envelope carry versions, and a reader rejects any other. Keep the action and the binary on one version, and regenerate with `callisto init` after an upgrade.\n\n## Not covered\n\n- Text output, stderr, warnings and the wording of error messages.\n- The library crates (`callisto-model`, `-manifests`, `-graph`). They are internal and version in lockstep with the CLI.\n- The order of keys in JSON output, and timing or performance.\n- Platforms without a published binary. Windows is not supported.\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"ff3dbb4e-f0f5-4b28-9071-3e2c79ca7714","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgMp4WVW2yGeY3XuKDFy8","requestRef":"581aa0de-2be0-4474-9eef-5448ed2883f8","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"2248bdde-4d5c-4edf-96cc-201850f3df50","timestamp":"2026-10-24T21:59:08.305Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"docs/stability","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
