{"parentUuid":"130b0dcd-ffa1-48cd-b14c-e410cf0e9c9e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"bd6ac0ce-389b-4193-aca8-c1bc4969277a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014fz9JSZUj8BMHsABVQLmF9","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/docs/stability.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"8dde65f8-dad4-4603-9e30-302269f9f5b6","timestamp":"2026-10-24T21:59:20.716Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/docs/stability.md","oldString":"`release plan`, `release execute`, `release artifact-manifest`, `release build-python`, `release-pr`,","newString":"`release plan`, `release inspect`, `release execute`, `release artifact-manifest`, `release build-python`, `release-pr`,","originalFile":"# Stability\n\nWhat Callisto promises to keep working from 1.0, and what it does not. A breaking change to anything in the first table needs a major version.\n\n## Stable\n\n| Surface | The promise |\n| --- | --- |\n| The eight commands (`add`, `status`, `version`, `pre`, `snapshot`, `init`, `release`, `completions`) and their flags | A flag keeps its meaning; a new flag never changes what the command did without it. |\n| Exit codes | `0` success, `1` failure, `2` usage error. |\n| `--format json` reports | Every report carries `schemaVersion`. Within a version a field is not removed, renamed or retyped; fields may be added. A shape change bumps the version. |\n| `callisto.toml` | A key keeps its meaning. Unknown keys are an error, so a new key arrives in a minor release and never changes an existing file's behavior. |\n| Changesets | The `.changeset/*.md` format and `pre.json` stay compatible with `@changesets/cli` for npm names; other ecosystems use `ecosystem/name` keys. |\n| Error codes | A code keeps naming the same condition and is never reused. New codes may appear. |\n| Tag names | `{name}@{version}` by default, `ecosystem/name@{version}` once another ecosystem has a package of that name. Pin a name with `tag-template` if a stable tag matters to your tooling. |\n| The GitHub Actions | The inputs of `callisto-action` and `setup-callisto`. The floating `v1` tag moves only on stable releases; pin a commit for a fixed version. |\n\n## CI plumbing\n\nThe generated workflows use `release plan`, `release execute`, `release artifact-manifest`, `release build-python`, `release-pr`, `matrix`, `compose-pr-body` and `schema`. They are hidden from `--help` and work only with the same Callisto version that generated them: the intent, decision, receipt and run envelope carry versions, and a reader rejects any other. Keep the action and the binary on one version, and regenerate with `callisto init` after an upgrade.\n\n## Not covered\n\n- Text output, stderr, warnings and the wording of error messages.\n- The library crates (`callisto-model`, `-manifests`, `-graph`). They are internal and version in lockstep with the CLI.\n- The order of keys in JSON output, and timing or performance.\n- Platforms without a published binary. Windows is not supported.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":17,"oldLines":7,"newStart":17,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," ## CI plumbing"," ","-The generated workflows use `release plan`, `release execute`, `release artifact-manifest`, `release build-python`, `release-pr`, `matrix`, `compose-pr-body` and `schema`. They are hidden from `--help` and work only with the same Callisto version that generated them: the intent, decision, receipt and run envelope carry versions, and a reader rejects any other. Keep the action and the binary on one version, and regenerate with `callisto init` after an upgrade.","+The generated workflows use `release plan`, `release inspect`, `release execute`, `release artifact-manifest`, `release build-python`, `release-pr`, `matrix`, `compose-pr-body` and `schema`. They are hidden from `--help` and work only with the same Callisto version that generated them: the intent, decision, receipt and run envelope carry versions, and a reader rejects any other. Keep the action and the binary on one version, and regenerate with `callisto init` after an upgrade."," "," ## Not covered"," "]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"130b0dcd-ffa1-48cd-b14c-e410cf0e9c9e","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"docs/stability","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
{"parentUuid":"8dde65f8-dad4-4603-9e30-302269f9f5b6","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Edit","toolUseID":"toolu_014fz9JSZUj8BMHsABVQLmF9","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"tool_complete\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"smoke-main\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Edit\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/gabe/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.1.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-post-tool-use.sh","durationMs":40},"type":"attachment","uuid":"f6b18b18-1519-4ad1-9b61-553aebe9e6d1","timestamp":"2026-10-24T21:59:20.715Z","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"docs/stability","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
{"parentUuid":"8f32dfa2-9a41-4f8c-941e-8acced751ed4","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"bd6ac0ce-389b-4193-aca8-c1bc4969277a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019TLkid8nwrs2kgsiTJt3ou","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/README.md has been updated successfully. (note: the file had been modified on disk since you last read it — the edit applied cleanly, but the file contains other changes not in your context. Read it before edits that depend on surrounding content.)"}]},"uuid":"af55ff71-8beb-4456-949d-238e59794051","timestamp":"2026-10-24T21:59:20.776Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/README.md","oldString":"Callisto is pre-v1. The [guide](docs/how-callisto-works.md) covers current support, known limits, and when another tool may be a better fit.","newString":"Callisto is pre-v1. The [guide](docs/how-callisto-works.md) covers current support, known limits, and when another tool may be a better fit, and [stability](docs/stability.md) says what will and will not change.","originalFile":"<p align=\"center\">\n  <picture>\n    <source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"assets/brand/hero-dark.png\">\n    <img src=\"assets/brand/hero-light.png\" alt=\"callisto, an Orin DX tool\" width=\"360\">\n  </picture>\n</p>\n\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <b>Dependency-aware, changeset-driven versioning and releases for Cargo, npm, and PyPI monorepos.</b>\n</p>\n\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <a href=\"https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto/actions/workflows/callisto-ci.yml\"><img src=\"https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto/actions/workflows/callisto-ci.yml/badge.svg\" alt=\"CI\" /></a>\n  <a href=\"LICENSE\"><img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT%20%2F%20FSL--1.1--MIT-blue.svg\" alt=\"License\" /></a>\n</p>\n\n---\n\nCallisto turns per-package changesets into a version plan for Cargo, npm/pnpm, and Python/PyPI workspaces. It reads native manifests to decide which dependents need updates, then prepares the files and release operations for review.\n\n## A change through Callisto\n\nSuppose `service` depends on a Cargo crate `core` at `^0.2`. A contributor records a minor change to `core`:\n\n```sh\ncallisto add --package cargo/core:minor --summary \"Add streaming API\"\ncallisto version --dry-run\n```\n\nWith the default cascade policy, the plan is:\n\n| Package | Before | Planned change |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `core` | `0.2.0` | `0.3.0` from the changeset |\n| `service` | `1.4.2`, requires `core ^0.2` | `1.4.3` from the default patch cascade; requirement updated to `^0.3` |\n| Unrelated npm or Python package | Its current version | No bump just because it shares the repo |\n\nThe dependency requirement triggers the `service` bump; sharing a repo does not. Callisto does not infer arbitrary cross-language dependencies. Explicit version groups can couple packages that should move together.\n\n- `callisto version` updates affected manifests, lockfiles, and changelogs for review and commit.\n- The release workflow uses native publishers and coordinates configured tags, GitHub releases, and assets. Package owners retain their hooks and credentials.\n\n```mermaid\n%%{init: {'theme': 'base', 'flowchart': {'curve': 'basis', 'nodeSpacing': 40, 'rankSpacing': 56}, 'themeVariables': {'fontFamily': 'Inter, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif', 'fontSize': '14px', 'lineColor': '#94a3b8', 'edgeLabelBackground': '#ffffff'}}}%%\nflowchart LR\n    classDef source fill:#eef2ff,stroke:#6366f1,stroke-width:1.5px,color:#1e1b4b,rx:10px,ry:10px,font-weight:600;\n    classDef store fill:#f8fafc,stroke:#64748b,stroke-width:1.5px,color:#0f172a,rx:10px,ry:10px;\n    classDef engine fill:#f5f3ff,stroke:#8b5cf6,stroke-width:1.5px,color:#4c1d95,rx:10px,ry:10px;\n    classDef router fill:#fffbeb,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:1.5px,color:#78350f,rx:10px,ry:10px,font-weight:600;\n    classDef output fill:#ecfdf5,stroke:#10b981,stroke-width:1.5px,color:#064e3b,rx:10px,ry:10px,font-weight:600;\n\n    changesets[\"<b>Changesets</b><br/>release intent\"] --> plan[\"<b>Version plan</b><br/>dependency-aware\"]\n    manifests[(\"<b>Native manifests</b><br/>Cargo · npm/pnpm · Python\")] --> plan\n    plan --> updates[\"<b>Version updates</b><br/>manifests · changelogs · lockfiles\"]\n    updates --> review{{\"<b>Review and commit</b><br/>versioned state\"}}\n    review --> release[\"<b>Release</b><br/>configured operations\"]\n    release --> outputs([\"Packages · tags · GitHub releases\"])\n\n    class changesets source\n    class manifests store\n    class plan,updates,release engine\n    class review router\n    class outputs output\n```\n\nCallisto is pre-v1. The [guide](docs/how-callisto-works.md) covers current support, known limits, and when another tool may be a better fit.\n\n## Install\n\n**proto** ([moonrepo/proto](https://moonrepo.dev/proto)), from a release binary:\n\n```toml\n# .prototools\n[plugins.tools]\ncallisto = \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/orin-dx/callisto/main/proto/callisto.toml\"\n```\n\n```bash\nproto install callisto\n```\n\n**cargo**, built from source (package `callisto-cli`, binary `callisto`):\n\n```bash\ncargo install callisto-cli\n```\n\n**Release binaries**, from [GitHub Releases](https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto/releases) (tag `callisto@<version>`):\n\n```bash\ncurl -sL \"https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto/releases/download/callisto@<version>/callisto-<target>.tar.gz\" | tar -xz\n```\n\nAvailable targets: `aarch64-apple-darwin`, `x86_64-apple-darwin`, `x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu`, `aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu`, `x86_64-unknown-linux-musl`.\n\n## Quick start\n\nStart in a Git repository with an `origin` push URL and crates.io credentials. This registry-only example publishes a crate and creates a tag; it does not build assets or create a GitHub Release. See [releasing](docs/releasing.md) for CI and product releases.\n\n```bash\n# 1. Scaffold callisto.toml and .changeset/ in the workspace root\ncallisto init --yes --no-workflow\n\n# 2. Record a pending change against a package\ncallisto add --package cargo/my-crate:minor --summary \"Add authentication middleware\"\n\n# 3. See pending changesets and the version bumps they imply\ncallisto status\n\n# 4. Commit the configuration and pending change\ngit add callisto.toml .changeset/\ngit commit -m \"chore: configure releases and record pending changes\"\n\n# 5. Consume changesets, bump manifests, update changelogs and lockfiles\ncallisto version\n\n# 6. Commit the staged release changes; release requires a clean checkout\ngit commit -m \"chore(release): version packages\"\n\n# 7. Preview, then publish\ncallisto release --dry-run\ncallisto release\n```\n\nRun `callisto --help` for prerelease mode, snapshots, CI checks, JSON output, and shell completions.\n\n## Documentation\n\n- [Guide](docs/how-callisto-works.md): release model, example, and supported layouts.\n- [Releasing](docs/releasing.md): local and CI workflows, limits, and recovery.\n- [Publishing](docs/publishing.md): registry credentials.\n- [Configuration](docs/config.md) and [errors](docs/errors.md): references.\n- [Contributing](CONTRIBUTING.md) and [security](SECURITY.md): project information.\n\n## License\n\nMixed: `callisto-model` is MIT; the rest of the workspace is [FSL-1.1-MIT](LICENSE) (becomes MIT two years after each version's release).\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":63,"oldLines":7,"newStart":63,"newLines":7,"lines":["     class outputs output"," ```"," ","-Callisto is pre-v1. The [guide](docs/how-callisto-works.md) covers current support, known limits, and when another tool may be a better fit.","+Callisto is pre-v1. The [guide](docs/how-callisto-works.md) covers current support, known limits, and when another tool may be a better fit, and [stability](docs/stability.md) says what will and will not change."," "," ## Install"," "]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"staleRecovered":true,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8f32dfa2-9a41-4f8c-941e-8acced751ed4","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"docs/stability","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
