{"parentUuid":"58a7ad43-eabb-4a15-b291-6ffb8de5c8ef","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMpNok5qDTAVfLp5gENd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NZv9jtGDZVyNhL2BxWqdSy","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-501/body_stability.md","content":"A one-page statement of what Callisto promises to keep working from 1.0, and what it does not. The review's point was that the contracts nobody can change later (tag names, report versions, config keys, error codes, action inputs) were never written down as promises, so a user could not tell what was covered. This writes them down, short.\n\n**This is a proposal for you to edit before merging.** Each row of the \"Stable\" table is a promise the project then has to keep, so it is the owner's call, not mine. In particular please check:\n\n- Exit codes `0` / `1` / `2` as the full set (the CLI uses no others today).\n- The tag rule. It states current behavior, including that a tag name becomes `ecosystem/name@version` once another ecosystem gets a package of the same name, and points at `tag-template` to pin one. Whether to keep that behavior or always qualify is a separate decision I have not made for you.\n- That the library crates are internal and outside the promise (already documented that way).\n- That hidden CI commands are supported only with a matching action and binary, not as a stable interface of their own. The wire-compat notes already say readers reject any other version.\n\nWhat I checked against the repo: the eight commands in `--help`, exit codes, the `schemaVersion` on reports, `deny_unknown_fields` on config, the floating `v1` tag moving only on stable releases, and the hidden command list. Linked from the README. Docs only; `just ci` passes.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1651,"cache_read_input_tokens":931255,"output_tokens":793,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1651,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":793,"cache_read_input_tokens":931255,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1651,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1651},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01NZv9jtGDZVyNhL2BxWqdSy":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-501/body_stability.md","content":"A one-page statement of what Callisto promises to keep working from 1.0, and what it does not. The review's point was that the contracts nobody can change later (tag names, report versions, config keys, error codes, action inputs) were never written down as promises, so a user could not tell what was covered. This writes them down, short.\n\n**This is a proposal for you to edit before merging.** Each row of the \"Stable\" table is a promise the project then has to keep, so it is the owner's call, not mine. In particular please check:\n\n- Exit codes `0` / `1` / `2` as the full set (the CLI uses no others today).\n- The tag rule. It states current behavior, including that a tag name becomes `ecosystem/name@version` once another ecosystem gets a package of the same name, and points at `tag-template` to pin one. Whether to keep that behavior or always qualify is a separate decision I have not made for you.\n- That the library crates are internal and outside the promise (already documented that way).\n- That hidden CI commands are supported only with a matching action and binary, not as a stable interface of their own. The wire-compat notes already say readers reject any other version.\n\nWhat I checked against the repo: the eight commands in `--help`, exit codes, the `schemaVersion` on reports, `deny_unknown_fields` on config, the floating `v1` tag moving only on stable releases, and the hidden command list. Linked from the README. Docs only; `just ci` passes.\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"7103df69-bbb2-4f51-b34c-a576c3712dc0","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgMpNoG4cERhCwrpS633J","requestRef":"50dd07e1-1064-42b2-8cf6-07f034790a46","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"09038ac7-17a5-4d1e-a197-c9c78e1cd9d3","timestamp":"2026-10-24T22:03:07.626Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"docs/stability","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
