{"parentUuid":"bee3d242-14cf-4afa-a82c-f51e42e851d8","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/docs/architecture/identity.md","snippet":""},"type":"attachment","uuid":"d5e2ed63-326f-4910-afd6-411f14442cf3","timestamp":"2026-10-24T22:03:59.943Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/docs/architecture/identity.md changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. The changes are not shown here; use Read if you need the current content.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
{"parentUuid":"d5e2ed63-326f-4910-afd6-411f14442cf3","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/docs/adr/0011-directory-keyed-package-identity.md","snippet":"1\t# 11. Packages are keyed by directory; promotion is display-only\n2\t\n3\tStatus: Accepted (implemented in #167)\n4\t\n5\t## Context\n6\t\n7\t- A package's id was its primary manifest name. When a second directory declared the same name in another ecosystem, walking promoted both to `cargo/foo` and `npm/foo` (`crates/callisto-graph/src/walk.rs`).\n8\t- Everything derived from the id changed with it. The default tag template was `{id}@{version}`, so an existing Cargo `foo` looked for `cargo/foo@*` tags, lost `foo@1.0.0`, and planned its next release from no prior tag.\n9\t- Selectors already tolerate promotion: `cargo/foo` resolves whether or not the package is promoted.\n10\t\n11\t## Decision\n12\t\n13\t- A package's stable identity is its workspace-relative directory: `Package::key() -> Option<PackageKey>` in `crates/callisto-model/src/package.rs`.\n14\t- `PackageId` is the display and selector form. Promotion changes only how it prints (`foo` becomes `cargo/foo`) and which bare selectors are ambiguous (E103).\n15\t- History recorded under a bare name follows the package that owned the name. Default tags are `{display id}@{version}` (`foo@1.0.0`, then `cargo/foo@1.1.0` once promoted), and a promoted package also finds `foo@*` tags whose commit contains its own manifest and no same-named package's. A bare `pre.json` key moves to the one same-named package that existed when `pre.json` was added. The CHANGELOG path comes from the directory.\n16\t- No configuration is needed. E101 is raised only when an explicit `tag-template` equals another package's default; E245 only when a bare `pre.json` key has no single owner.\n17\t\n18\t## Options considered\n19\t\n20\t- **Primary manifest name as key** — rejected: promotion changed the id, and with it the tag lookup of an already-released package.\n21\t- **Re-key every in-run map by `PackageKey`** — rejected for now: about 66 maps over roughly 1,000 `PackageId` uses. Promotion is computed once per walk, so within a run `PackageId` maps one-to-one onto `PackageKey`; re-keying would change no behavior.\n22\t- **Default tags from the native name (`foo@{version}`) for every package** — rejected: promoted `cargo/foo` and `npm/foo` would share tags, so one of them needed a `tag-template` (E101), and already-promoted workspaces would change their tag names.\n23\t- **Fall back to `{name}@` tags without an ownership check** — rejected: the newly added package would adopt the old one's releases.\n24\t\n25\t## Consequences\n26\t\n27\t- Adding a same-named package in another ecosystem no longer changes the existing package's tags, CHANGELOG or pre-release baseline.\n28\t- Workspaces that are already promoted keep their `cargo/foo@*` tags unchanged.\n29\t- Ownership costs one `git rev-parse` per candidate tag of a promoted package.\n30\t- A pending changeset that names the bare `foo` is ambiguous after promotion (E103, WS-ID-06) and must be qualified.\n31\t\n32\t## Enforcement\n33\t\n34\t- `TagTemplate::default_for` in `crates/callisto-model/src/tag.rs`; the ownership fallback in `TagIndex::build` (`crates/callisto-graph/src/tags.rs`); `assign_promoted_pre_keys` in `crates/callisto-graph/src/lib.rs`.\n35\t- `promotion_changes_the_display_id_but_not_the_key` in `crates/callisto-graph/src/walk.rs`; `crates/callisto-cli/tests/identity_promotion_tests.rs`.\n...\n37\t\n38\t## Revisit when\n39\t\n40\t- Something persists a package reference that is not a selector, tag or path, such as a cache keyed by package. It should use `PackageKey`.\n41\t- A package can move directories while keeping its identity.\n42\t\n43\t## Sources\n44\t\n45\t- Owner decision, `docs/projects/ROAD-TO-V1.md` \"v1 fix plan\" decisions (2026-09-25)\n46\t- #167 (\"refactor(identity)!: key packages by directory; promotion is display-only\") and its zero-config follow-up"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"4f7e16fa-fbe5-4a42-b15d-7700a431ceab","timestamp":"2026-10-24T22:03:59.943Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/docs/adr/0011-directory-keyed-package-identity.md changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. Here are the relevant changes (shown with line numbers):\n1\t# 11. Packages are keyed by directory; promotion is display-only\n2\t\n3\tStatus: Accepted (implemented in #167)\n4\t\n5\t## Context\n6\t\n7\t- A package's id was its primary manifest name. When a second directory declared the same name in another ecosystem, walking promoted both to `cargo/foo` and `npm/foo` (`crates/callisto-graph/src/walk.rs`).\n8\t- Everything derived from the id changed with it. The default tag template was `{id}@{version}`, so an existing Cargo `foo` looked for `cargo/foo@*` tags, lost `foo@1.0.0`, and planned its next release from no prior tag.\n9\t- Selectors already tolerate promotion: `cargo/foo` resolves whether or not the package is promoted.\n10\t\n11\t## Decision\n12\t\n13\t- A package's stable identity is its workspace-relative directory: `Package::key() -> Option<PackageKey>` in `crates/callisto-model/src/package.rs`.\n14\t- `PackageId` is the display and selector form. Promotion changes only how it prints (`foo` becomes `cargo/foo`) and which bare selectors are ambiguous (E103).\n15\t- History recorded under a bare name follows the package that owned the name. Default tags are `{display id}@{version}` (`foo@1.0.0`, then `cargo/foo@1.1.0` once promoted), and a promoted package also finds `foo@*` tags whose commit contains its own manifest and no same-named package's. A bare `pre.json` key moves to the one same-named package that existed when `pre.json` was added. The CHANGELOG path comes from the directory.\n16\t- No configuration is needed. E101 is raised only when an explicit `tag-template` equals another package's default; E245 only when a bare `pre.json` key has no single owner.\n17\t\n18\t## Options considered\n19\t\n20\t- **Primary manifest name as key** — rejected: promotion changed the id, and with it the tag lookup of an already-released package.\n21\t- **Re-key every in-run map by `PackageKey`** — rejected for now: about 66 maps over roughly 1,000 `PackageId` uses. Promotion is computed once per walk, so within a run `PackageId` maps one-to-one onto `PackageKey`; re-keying would change no behavior.\n22\t- **Default tags from the native name (`foo@{version}`) for every package** — rejected: promoted `cargo/foo` and `npm/foo` would share tags, so one of them needed a `tag-template` (E101), and already-promoted workspaces would change their tag names.\n23\t- **Fall back to `{name}@` tags without an ownership check** — rejected: the newly added package would adopt the old one's releases.\n24\t\n25\t## Consequences\n26\t\n27\t- Adding a same-named package in another ecosystem no longer changes the existing package's tags, CHANGELOG or pre-release baseline.\n28\t- Workspaces that are already promoted keep their `cargo/foo@*` tags unchanged.\n29\t- Ownership costs one `git rev-parse` per candidate tag of a promoted package.\n30\t- A pending changeset that names the bare `foo` is ambiguous after promotion (E103, WS-ID-06) and must be qualified.\n31\t\n32\t## Enforcement\n33\t\n34\t- `TagTemplate::default_for` in `crates/callisto-model/src/tag.rs`; the ownership fallback in `TagIndex::build` (`crates/callisto-graph/src/tags.rs`); `assign_promoted_pre_keys` in `crates/callisto-graph/src/lib.rs`.\n35\t- `promotion_changes_the_display_id_but_not_the_key` in `crates/callisto-graph/src/walk.rs`; `crates/callisto-cli/tests/identity_promotion_tests.rs`.\n...\n37\t\n38\t## Revisit when\n39\t\n40\t- Something persists a package reference that is not a selector, tag or path, such as a cache keyed by package. It should use `PackageKey`.\n41\t- A package can move directories while keeping its identity.\n42\t\n43\t## Sources\n44\t\n45\t- Owner decision, `docs/projects/ROAD-TO-V1.md` \"v1 fix plan\" decisions (2026-09-25)\n46\t- #167 (\"refactor(identity)!: key packages by directory; promotion is display-only\") and its zero-config follow-up\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
{"parentUuid":"4f7e16fa-fbe5-4a42-b15d-7700a431ceab","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/docs/adr/0010-native-resolution-after-version.md","snippet":"1\t# 10. The workspace resolves natively after `version` or `snapshot`\n2\t\n3\tStatus: Proposed\n4\t\n5\t## Context\n6\t\n7\t- 0.7.2 shipped `callisto-cli` requiring `callisto-graph = \"0.7.0\"`: the spec still covered the released version, so the out-of-range-only cascade left the floor unraised.\n8\t- `cargo metadata --locked`, `npm ci`, `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` and `uv lock --check` fail whenever a manifest and its lockfile disagree, whether the spec is stale or the lockfile is.\n9\t- `snapshot` only rewrites specs a patch bump would break, so a minor or major snapshot bump leaves a covering-but-stale spec in place and `cargo metadata` fails after it.\n10\t\n11\t## Decision\n...\n31\t- VER-CAS-01 and VER-CAS-06 in `docs/specs/versioning.json`.\n32\t\n33\t## Revisit when\n34\t\n35\t- A dependent needs to pin below its dependency's newly released version on purpose (e.g. a deliberate compatibility window); today's rule always raises the floor.\n36\t\n37\t## Sources\n38\t\n39\t- Owner decision, `docs/projects/ROAD-TO-V1.md` \"v1 fix plan\" decisions (2026-09-25)\n40\t- The fix in this PR: raising the floor of co-released dependents in `cascade.rs`"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"a83ec20e-cb27-46f8-a26b-2249da05e44d","timestamp":"2026-10-24T22:03:59.943Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/docs/adr/0010-native-resolution-after-version.md changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. Here are the relevant changes (shown with line numbers):\n1\t# 10. The workspace resolves natively after `version` or `snapshot`\n2\t\n3\tStatus: Proposed\n4\t\n5\t## Context\n6\t\n7\t- 0.7.2 shipped `callisto-cli` requiring `callisto-graph = \"0.7.0\"`: the spec still covered the released version, so the out-of-range-only cascade left the floor unraised.\n8\t- `cargo metadata --locked`, `npm ci`, `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` and `uv lock --check` fail whenever a manifest and its lockfile disagree, whether the spec is stale or the lockfile is.\n9\t- `snapshot` only rewrites specs a patch bump would break, so a minor or major snapshot bump leaves a covering-but-stale spec in place and `cargo metadata` fails after it.\n10\t\n11\t## Decision\n...\n31\t- VER-CAS-01 and VER-CAS-06 in `docs/specs/versioning.json`.\n32\t\n33\t## Revisit when\n34\t\n35\t- A dependent needs to pin below its dependency's newly released version on purpose (e.g. a deliberate compatibility window); today's rule always raises the floor.\n36\t\n37\t## Sources\n38\t\n39\t- Owner decision, `docs/projects/ROAD-TO-V1.md` \"v1 fix plan\" decisions (2026-09-25)\n40\t- The fix in this PR: raising the floor of co-released dependents in `cascade.rs`\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
{"parentUuid":"a83ec20e-cb27-46f8-a26b-2249da05e44d","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/docs/adr/0009-tag-identity-is-commit-and-annotation.md","snippet":"1\t# 9. A tag's identity is its commit and being annotated\n2\t\n3\tStatus: Proposed\n4\t\n5\t## Context\n6\t\n7\t- A rerun adopts effects that already landed (ADR 3), so it must decide whether an existing tag is the one it planned.\n8\t- The local check read the tag with `git for-each-ref` and compared the target commit and the annotation text. The remote check uses `git ls-remote`, which returns the tag object and peeled commit but not the annotation text, so it compared only the commit.\n9\t- The same repository state could therefore be adopted or rejected depending on whether the remote tag had been fetched.\n10\t\n11\t## Decision\n...\n28\t- REL-RERUN-02 and REL-RERUN-03 in `docs/specs/release.json`.\n29\t\n30\t## Revisit when\n31\t\n32\t- Something downstream starts reading the annotation text (release notes, signing policy, provenance).\n33\t\n34\t## Sources\n35\t\n36\t- Owner decision, `docs/projects/ROAD-TO-V1.md` \"v1 fix plan\" decisions (2026-09-25)\n37\t- The fix in this PR: \"fix: stop comparing tag annotation text in release rerun observation\""},"type":"attachment","uuid":"2d9d2b62-6ddb-4491-9cec-6c987b5fa8a7","timestamp":"2026-10-24T22:03:59.944Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/docs/adr/0009-tag-identity-is-commit-and-annotation.md changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. Here are the relevant changes (shown with line numbers):\n1\t# 9. A tag's identity is its commit and being annotated\n2\t\n3\tStatus: Proposed\n4\t\n5\t## Context\n6\t\n7\t- A rerun adopts effects that already landed (ADR 3), so it must decide whether an existing tag is the one it planned.\n8\t- The local check read the tag with `git for-each-ref` and compared the target commit and the annotation text. The remote check uses `git ls-remote`, which returns the tag object and peeled commit but not the annotation text, so it compared only the commit.\n9\t- The same repository state could therefore be adopted or rejected depending on whether the remote tag had been fetched.\n10\t\n11\t## Decision\n...\n28\t- REL-RERUN-02 and REL-RERUN-03 in `docs/specs/release.json`.\n29\t\n30\t## Revisit when\n31\t\n32\t- Something downstream starts reading the annotation text (release notes, signing policy, provenance).\n33\t\n34\t## Sources\n35\t\n36\t- Owner decision, `docs/projects/ROAD-TO-V1.md` \"v1 fix plan\" decisions (2026-09-25)\n37\t- The fix in this PR: \"fix: stop comparing tag annotation text in release rerun observation\"\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
{"parentUuid":"2d9d2b62-6ddb-4491-9cec-6c987b5fa8a7","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/docs/adr/0007-platform-packages-owned-through-optional-dependencies.md","snippet":""},"type":"attachment","uuid":"70173200-ecea-4ffd-b0dd-83d15c43ceff","timestamp":"2026-10-24T22:03:59.944Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/docs/adr/0007-platform-packages-owned-through-optional-dependencies.md changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. The changes are not shown here; use Read if you need the current content.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
{"parentUuid":"70173200-ecea-4ffd-b0dd-83d15c43ceff","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/docs/adr/0005-system-git-only.md","snippet":"18\t- **gix only** — not considered in #145. Reason not recorded.\n19\t\n20\t## Consequences\n21\t\n22\t- History walks use `git log --no-merges --full-history`, matching the gix commit sets; plain `git log` history simplification drops commits whose change a later merge discarded.\n23\t- Callisto depends on the installed git version and parses its output.\n24\t- Annotated tags work on runners with no git identity: the tagger falls back to the target commit's committer (#145).\n25\t- The managed release-PR action is outside this decision: it writes its commit and branch refs through the GitHub API (`.github/actions/callisto-action/scripts/create-or-update-release-pr.sh`).\n26\t- Today `release-pr commit-plan` reads staged bytes from the worktree, not the index (docs/projects/ROAD-TO-V1.md, v1 fix plan §1).\n27\t\n28\t## Enforcement\n29\t\n30\t- `callisto_model::vcs` has no gix dependency and one `GitAccess` type (`crates/callisto-model/src/vcs/access.rs`).\n31\t- Nothing bans gix in `deny.toml`; reintroducing it needs a new ADR.\n32\t\n33\t## Revisit when\n34\t"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"e0becf6c-133d-4107-8220-07481fe8e924","timestamp":"2026-10-24T22:03:59.944Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/docs/adr/0005-system-git-only.md changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. Here are the relevant changes (shown with line numbers):\n18\t- **gix only** — not considered in #145. Reason not recorded.\n19\t\n20\t## Consequences\n21\t\n22\t- History walks use `git log --no-merges --full-history`, matching the gix commit sets; plain `git log` history simplification drops commits whose change a later merge discarded.\n23\t- Callisto depends on the installed git version and parses its output.\n24\t- Annotated tags work on runners with no git identity: the tagger falls back to the target commit's committer (#145).\n25\t- The managed release-PR action is outside this decision: it writes its commit and branch refs through the GitHub API (`.github/actions/callisto-action/scripts/create-or-update-release-pr.sh`).\n26\t- Today `release-pr commit-plan` reads staged bytes from the worktree, not the index (docs/projects/ROAD-TO-V1.md, v1 fix plan §1).\n27\t\n28\t## Enforcement\n29\t\n30\t- `callisto_model::vcs` has no gix dependency and one `GitAccess` type (`crates/callisto-model/src/vcs/access.rs`).\n31\t- Nothing bans gix in `deny.toml`; reintroducing it needs a new ADR.\n32\t\n33\t## Revisit when\n34\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
{"parentUuid":"e0becf6c-133d-4107-8220-07481fe8e924","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/docs/adr/0004-ecosystem-tools-publish-and-own-auth.md","snippet":"13\t\n14\t## Options considered\n15\t\n16\t- **Native registry clients in callisto** — rejected. The original design argued the tools \"already do registry auth, retries, rate-limit handling, and idempotence — reimplementing any of that inside callisto would be redundant and would put callisto in the business of tracking every registry's quirks\" (docs/00-design.md §9). §9.5 dropped `octocrab`/`reqwest`/`tokio` from the CLI, which \"significantly shrinks the CLI's dependency surface\".\n17\t- **Credential pre-flight before the first effect** — added in #134, removed in #143: \"cargo, npm, twine and gh report their own auth failures, and a rerun adopts every effect that already landed, so a second credential model in Callisto only drifts from the tools'\".\n18\t\n19\t## Consequences\n20\t\n21\t- Any auth method a tool supports works without callisto modelling it.\n22\t- A missing credential surfaces mid-release as E163 (E164 for `gh`), carrying the tool's redacted stderr. Effects before it have landed; a rerun adopts them (ADR 3).\n23\t- Callisto parses tool output to classify results (for example \"already published\"), so a tool's output change can break classification (`crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/registry_argv.rs`).\n24\t- Every release machine needs the tools on `PATH`.\n25\t- Today observation timeouts and spawn failures skip the retry loop, and PyPI ignores `Retry-After` (docs/projects/ROAD-TO-V1.md, v1 fix plan §1).\n26\t\n27\t## Enforcement\n28\t\n29\t- None automated. The fixed programs are in `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/release/provider/policy.rs` (`programs`: git, gh, cargo, npm, curl); the publish programs (pnpm, yarn, bun, `python3` or `python`, twine) are built in `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/registry_argv.rs`.\n30\t- No HTTP client crate (`reqwest`, `ureq`, `octocrab`, `hyper`) appears in `Cargo.lock`; nothing checks this.\n31\t\n32\t## Revisit when\n33\t"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"c38b774c-23ad-4552-a9c7-12462b360854","timestamp":"2026-10-24T22:03:59.944Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/docs/adr/0004-ecosystem-tools-publish-and-own-auth.md changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. Here are the relevant changes (shown with line numbers):\n13\t\n14\t## Options considered\n15\t\n16\t- **Native registry clients in callisto** — rejected. The original design argued the tools \"already do registry auth, retries, rate-limit handling, and idempotence — reimplementing any of that inside callisto would be redundant and would put callisto in the business of tracking every registry's quirks\" (docs/00-design.md §9). §9.5 dropped `octocrab`/`reqwest`/`tokio` from the CLI, which \"significantly shrinks the CLI's dependency surface\".\n17\t- **Credential pre-flight before the first effect** — added in #134, removed in #143: \"cargo, npm, twine and gh report their own auth failures, and a rerun adopts every effect that already landed, so a second credential model in Callisto only drifts from the tools'\".\n18\t\n19\t## Consequences\n20\t\n21\t- Any auth method a tool supports works without callisto modelling it.\n22\t- A missing credential surfaces mid-release as E163 (E164 for `gh`), carrying the tool's redacted stderr. Effects before it have landed; a rerun adopts them (ADR 3).\n23\t- Callisto parses tool output to classify results (for example \"already published\"), so a tool's output change can break classification (`crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/registry_argv.rs`).\n24\t- Every release machine needs the tools on `PATH`.\n25\t- Today observation timeouts and spawn failures skip the retry loop, and PyPI ignores `Retry-After` (docs/projects/ROAD-TO-V1.md, v1 fix plan §1).\n26\t\n27\t## Enforcement\n28\t\n29\t- None automated. The fixed programs are in `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/release/provider/policy.rs` (`programs`: git, gh, cargo, npm, curl); the publish programs (pnpm, yarn, bun, `python3` or `python`, twine) are built in `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/registry_argv.rs`.\n30\t- No HTTP client crate (`reqwest`, `ureq`, `octocrab`, `hyper`) appears in `Cargo.lock`; nothing checks this.\n31\t\n32\t## Revisit when\n33\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
{"parentUuid":"c38b774c-23ad-4552-a9c7-12462b360854","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/docs/adr/0003-reruns-adopt-landed-effects.md","snippet":""},"type":"attachment","uuid":"ef7a0a35-88fe-4520-8bdd-99b357fae1ae","timestamp":"2026-10-24T22:03:59.944Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/docs/adr/0003-reruns-adopt-landed-effects.md changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. The changes are not shown here; use Read if you need the current content.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
{"parentUuid":"ef7a0a35-88fe-4520-8bdd-99b357fae1ae","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/docs/adr/0001-changesets-compatible-change-records.md","snippet":"17\t- **Conventional Commits as the primary input** — rejected. That is release-please's model, \"the default choice for a team starting from scratch\"; callisto does not try to out-build it. The changesets user base \"dislikes Conventional-Commits-only tools\" (docs/00-design.md §3.2). Inference is kept as an opt-in trigger, and P1's rollback guarantee covers only `Changeset`-trigger packages (§4 P1 scope note).\n18\t- **A callisto-specific format** — rejected: adoption and rollback must each be one commit, so existing `.changeset/` files have to keep working in both directions (\"One-commit adoption, one-commit rollback. This is the adoption gate; nothing overrides it\", docs/00-design.md §4 P1).\n19\t\n20\t## Consequences\n21\t\n22\t- Adopting callisto is meant to be one commit; leaving it is lossless only for `changeset`-trigger packages, since `auto` packages have no changesets equivalent to roll back to (docs/00-design.md §4 P1 scope note). See the gaps below.\n23\t- Callisto inherits `@changesets/cli`'s semantics, including the rigid `bump_version` (no 0.x remap on an explicit major; docs/00-design.md §6.2). The opt-in pre-major remap lives in inference only, never in `bump_version` (docs/00-design.md §7.1).\n24\t- If `@changesets/cli` ships native polyglot support (its issue #665), callisto's positioning narrows (docs/00-design.md §3.2).\n25\t- Today's code falls short of full compatibility: an empty changeset is rejected (E048), a versionless private root `package.json` fails (E013), `pre enter` after `pre exit` is rejected, and a changeset with one unknown entry is consumed (docs/projects/ROAD-TO-V1.md, v1 fix plan §4).\n26\t\n27\t## Enforcement\n28\t\n29\t- Parser and writer tests, including a write-then-parse proptest: `crates/callisto-model/src/format/changeset/tests.rs`.\n30\t- Bump arithmetic tests: `crates/callisto-model/src/format/bump.rs`.\n31\t- No test runs against `@changesets/cli`; compatibility rests on hand-written unit cases.\n32\t\n33\t## Revisit when\n...\n36\t- `@changesets/cli` ships native polyglot support (#665).\n37\t- The owner decides callisto should target Conventional-Commits-first teams.\n38\t\n39\t## Sources\n40\t\n41\t- docs/00-design.md §0, §3.1, §3.2, §4 (P1), §6.2, §7.1 (deleted in 11038b11b; read with `git show 11038b11b^:docs/00-design.md`)\n42\t- PR #143 (bde7305f9): inference always compiled in, gated only by `release-trigger`\n43\t- `docs/specs/versioning.json` VER-AGG-01; `crates/callisto-graph/src/aggregate.rs`\n44\t- docs/projects/ROAD-TO-V1.md, v1 fix plan §4"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"25597b9e-a125-4891-a6d9-c0a4288ec850","timestamp":"2026-10-24T22:03:59.945Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/docs/adr/0001-changesets-compatible-change-records.md changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. Here are the relevant changes (shown with line numbers):\n17\t- **Conventional Commits as the primary input** — rejected. That is release-please's model, \"the default choice for a team starting from scratch\"; callisto does not try to out-build it. The changesets user base \"dislikes Conventional-Commits-only tools\" (docs/00-design.md §3.2). Inference is kept as an opt-in trigger, and P1's rollback guarantee covers only `Changeset`-trigger packages (§4 P1 scope note).\n18\t- **A callisto-specific format** — rejected: adoption and rollback must each be one commit, so existing `.changeset/` files have to keep working in both directions (\"One-commit adoption, one-commit rollback. This is the adoption gate; nothing overrides it\", docs/00-design.md §4 P1).\n19\t\n20\t## Consequences\n21\t\n22\t- Adopting callisto is meant to be one commit; leaving it is lossless only for `changeset`-trigger packages, since `auto` packages have no changesets equivalent to roll back to (docs/00-design.md §4 P1 scope note). See the gaps below.\n23\t- Callisto inherits `@changesets/cli`'s semantics, including the rigid `bump_version` (no 0.x remap on an explicit major; docs/00-design.md §6.2). The opt-in pre-major remap lives in inference only, never in `bump_version` (docs/00-design.md §7.1).\n24\t- If `@changesets/cli` ships native polyglot support (its issue #665), callisto's positioning narrows (docs/00-design.md §3.2).\n25\t- Today's code falls short of full compatibility: an empty changeset is rejected (E048), a versionless private root `package.json` fails (E013), `pre enter` after `pre exit` is rejected, and a changeset with one unknown entry is consumed (docs/projects/ROAD-TO-V1.md, v1 fix plan §4).\n26\t\n27\t## Enforcement\n28\t\n29\t- Parser and writer tests, including a write-then-parse proptest: `crates/callisto-model/src/format/changeset/tests.rs`.\n30\t- Bump arithmetic tests: `crates/callisto-model/src/format/bump.rs`.\n31\t- No test runs against `@changesets/cli`; compatibility rests on hand-written unit cases.\n32\t\n33\t## Revisit when\n...\n36\t- `@changesets/cli` ships native polyglot support (#665).\n37\t- The owner decides callisto should target Conventional-Commits-first teams.\n38\t\n39\t## Sources\n40\t\n41\t- docs/00-design.md §0, §3.1, §3.2, §4 (P1), §6.2, §7.1 (deleted in 11038b11b; read with `git show 11038b11b^:docs/00-design.md`)\n42\t- PR #143 (bde7305f9): inference always compiled in, gated only by `release-trigger`\n43\t- `docs/specs/versioning.json` VER-AGG-01; `crates/callisto-graph/src/aggregate.rs`\n44\t- docs/projects/ROAD-TO-V1.md, v1 fix plan §4\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
