{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","hash":"1556e624a61b1626166c819119d23653c4274f354a1ef87dd42888278c75d7f1","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"CI passes (exit 0, 631 unit tests, coverage 92.9%). Shipping the PR now."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VDvpAEJ7ycBqoRo1dP9MXk","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main && printf 'npm ranges written with spaces between comparators (`>=1.0.0 <2.0.0`, `1.0.0 - 2.0.0`) were skipped silently, so a dependent kept declaring compatibility with a version the release left behind.\\n\\nThey now parse as ranges, so `version` stops with E319 before writing when a release takes the dependency out of one. Comma-separated ranges are unchanged.\\n\\nTests: unit cases for spaced, hyphen, operator-spaced, `||` and comma forms; an end-to-end cascade test that checks the manifest is untouched after E319.\\n' > /tmp/claude-501/body-npmspace.md && /tmp/claude-501/ship.sh fix/npm-space-ranges origin/main \"fix(version): read npm ranges written with spaces\" /tmp/claude-501/body-npmspace.md \"Read npm ranges written with spaces between comparators as one range.\" . 2>&1 | tail -8","description":"Commit, push and open the PR","dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
